2 CONT WordPerfect
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashton began his work in computer science in the University of Utah, studying computing and music in the early 1970s. In 1977 Ashton began work on word processing when he created a spec for an improved console-based word processor
2 CONC . His spec outlined various innovations at the time, including continuous documents, function key shortcuts, modeless editing, and primitive WYSIWYG formatting. Along with Bruce Bastian, his student, Ashton incorporated Satellite 
2 CONC Software International, which would later become WordPerfect Corporation, in September 1979. In 1987, Ashton left BYU to serve full-time as president and CEO of WordPerfect Corporation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashton ran WordPerfect as a triumvirate, along with Bastian and W.E. (“Pete”) Peterson. Ashton and Bastian each controlled 49.5% of the company, and Peterson controlled 1%. While Ashton was the titular head of WordPerfect, Peterso
2 CONC n ran the day-to-day operations, and was frequently misinterpreted as the head of the company by the press. Ashton's management style was hands-off. At one point, the entire development organization of WordPerfect reported directl
2 CONC y to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1990 Ashton was identified by Forbes magazine as one of the 400 wealthiest individuals in the U.S.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashton joined the Novell Corporation Board of Directors in 1994, and resigned in 1996.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashton is unrelated to Ashton-Tate, a database company and contemporary of WordPerfect in the 1980s. Ashton is the grandson of late LDS Church president David O. McKay. Ashton served as a Mormon missionary in Central Germany as a 
2 CONC young man. Ashton is an Eagle Scout and was awarded the Distinguished Eagle Scout Award through Boy Scouts of America's Utah National Parks Council in 1993.
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1999, Ashton founded ASH Capital, a venture investment company controlled by Ashton and managed by James Savas and David Harkness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanksgiving Point
2 CONT
2 CONT After WordPerfect was acquired by Novell and Ashton’s responsibilities were alleviated, he and his wife founded Thanksgiving Point. Thanksgiving Point is located in Lehi, Utah, within 20 miles of WordPerfect’s former corporate hea
2 CONC dquarters in Orem.
2 CONT
2 CONT “We wanted to create something for the people around us," says Ashton. "We've been blessed financially and with a large family. We wanted to give something back to the community and the families in our area.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Today, Thanksgiving Point provides the community with a place where adults and children can learn about farming, gardening and cooking. It also has a championship caliber golf course, a museum of ancient life and a movie theater.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mission President
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashton served as a mission president for LDS Church in western Ontario from July 2004 through June 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT California Prop 8
2 CONT
2 CONT The California Proposition 8 campaign announced that a US$1 million donation to support Proposition 8 was given by Ashton. The donation was reported by the Prop 8 campaign on October 28, 2008. Ashton's former business partner, Bru
2 CONC ce Bastian, who is openly gay, gave $1 million to oppose Proposition 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Proposition_8_(2008)
