1 NAME Christian Wilford /Kunz/
2 GIVN Christian Wilford
2 _MARNM Kunz
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1878
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1907
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Christian Wilford "CW"Kunz was born on November 10, 1878, at Bern, Bear Lake County, Idaho, to Christian Kunz and Eliza Buehler.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was called on an LDS Mission to Germany, and died in Germany on June 7, 1907, and was buried in Berlin, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT The other photo shown under the Media Tab shows his entire family, but since he was not pictured in the photo, it must have been taken after his death in 1907.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the appearance of that photo, it was taken perhaps around 1918, since their son Seymour in the third row is wearing a uniform typical of those from WWI.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Kunz Family copy courtesy of Paul Anthon-Nielson. Christian Kunz Family Courtesy of Zina Kunz Hatch Fuit Cox
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Group-Front Row: Charlotte, Zina, Adeline, and Lydia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seond Row: David C. (D.C.), Caroline B. (second wife of Christian and his first wife, Eliza's, sister),  Christian (father),  Eliza, (first wife of Christian) and daughter, Eliza Rebecca (Lizzie R.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Third Row: Magdalena (Maggie), Seymour, Henry (Harry), Frank, Anthon (Tony), and Ida. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth Row: Seth, Alma, John M., and Smith.
