1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Heber Chase Kimball''' (June 14, 1801 – June 22, 1868) was a leader in the early Latter Day Saint movement. He served as one of the original twelve apostles in the early Mormon church, and as first counselor to Brigham Youn
2 CONC g in the First Presidency of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints from 1847 until his death..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Kimball was born to Solomon Farnham Kimball and Anna Spaulding in Sheldon, Franklin County, Vermont. Kimball's forefathers arrived in America from England in the early 17th century, and some family members participated in the 
2 CONC Revolutionary War. His immediate family consisted of Charles Spaulding Kimball, Eliza Kimball, Abigail Kimball, Heber Chase Kimball, Melvina Kimball, Solomon Kimball and Daniel Spaulding Kimball. All were born in Sheldon. Daniel d
2 CONC ied at the age of seven months. Heber Chase was named after a Judge Chase, who had helped the family in their efforts to settle in the area..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Heber C. Kimball died on June 22, 1868, at age 67, in Salt Lake City, Utah, from the effects of a carriage accident. He was buried in the Kimball-Whitney Cemetery..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heber_C._Kimball
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriages==
