1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Utah Pioneer Dies At Ogden -- Death Ends Long Service in L.D.S. Church for Elnathan Eldredge
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogden--Elnathan Eldredge, 89, well-known Utah pioneer, who for many years had charge of immigrants crossing the plains to Utah, died Tuesday night at 12 O'clock at the home of his daughter, Mrs. E. C. Stratford, 1183 Twenty-eighth
2 CONC  street.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born September 12, 1841, in Dennis, Massachusetts, the son of Elnathan and Ruth Baker Eldredge.  He is a direct descendant of William Brewster of the Mayflower.  He came with his parents across the plains in 1847, arriving 
2 CONC in Salt Lake valley September 26, and was appointed by the Latter-day Saint church to be in charge of immigration across the plains in 1861.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Eldredge was called on a mission to Europe in 1863 and labored for a time in the Manchester conference.  In 1864 he was appointed president of the Preston conference and in 1866, at the end of his mission, he was appointed to 
2 CONC take charge of the companies of Latter-day Saints converts as they arrived in America.  He guided 5,000 people to Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1869 he was named, with several other young men, to colonize the Bear Lake valley.  While there, from 1869 to 1874, he had a government contract to carry mail from St. Charles, Idaho, to Evanston, Wyoming.  In 1878 he helped co
2 CONC lonize St. John, Arizona.  He served a mission in Indiana in 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his widow, Mrs. Mary Eldredge, and two brothers, Joshua Eldredge and Joseph U. Eldredge Sr., of Salt Lake City, and seven daughters and four sons, Mrs. W. E. Wread, Pasadena, California; Mrs. E. C. Stratford, Ogden; 
2 CONC Mrs. W. S. Wieler, Mrs. John Johnson, E. Roscoe Eldredge, Mrs. Ernest S. Holmes, Lawrence Eldredge, Seymour Eldredge, all of Salt Lake City; Mrs. H. W. Burton, Los Angeles; Harold O. Eldredge, Pasadena, California; Mrs. Maurice Gr
2 CONC iffin, Los Angeles; 34 grandchildren and 12 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 1 p.m. Sunday in the Seventeenth ward in Ogden, under the direction of Larkin & Sons.  Interment will be made in Salt Lake City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Salt Lake Tribune, Apr. 23, 1931
2 CONT [transcribed and proofread by David Grow, Jan. 2006]
2 CONT **************************************************
2 CONT Funeral Set for Pioneer
2 CONT Ogden--Funeral services for Elnathan Eldredge, 89, well-known Utah pioneer, who died Wednesday will be held Sunday, April 25, at 1 p.m. in the Seventeenth ward chapel, with Bishop Charles H. Halverson in charge.  Interment will be
2 CONC  in the Salt Lake City cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Eldredge is survived, besides his widow and two brothers, by four sons and seven daughters: Mrs. W. E. Wread, Pasadena, California; Mrs. E. C. Stratford, Ogden; Mrs. W. S. Wieler, Mrs. John Johnson, E. Roscoe Eldredge, Mrs. Er
2 CONC nest S. Holmes, Lawrence Eldredge, Seymour Eldredge, all of Salt Lake City; Mrs. H. W. Burton, Los Angeles; Harold O. Eldredge, Pasadena, California; Mrs. Maurice Griffin, Los Angeles; 34 grandchildren and 12 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deseret News, Apr. 24, 1931
