2 CONC  became a member of the 19th quorum of Seventy. He left Nauvoo as an exile together with the rest of the Saints in 1846, and reached Great Salt Lake Valley in 1848. Together with a few other settlers he spent the first winter near
2 CONC  the mouth of North Canyon in Davis county, about one mile south of Bountiful, and located in 1849 at Farmington, where he resided during there remainder of his life. When he crossed the plains in 1848 his earthly possessions amou
2 CONC nted to a very little, but by industry and hard labor he succeeded in acquiring considerable property. In 1856-1858 he filled a successful mission to Great Britain. In the year 1869 he went to the States after the remains of his s
