1 NAME Ezra Alpheus /Chipman/
2 GIVN Ezra Alpheus
2 SURN Chipman
2 _MARNM Chipman
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 OCT 1817
2 PLAC Johnstown, Hastings County, Ontario, Canada
2 ADDR
3 CITY Johnstown
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 BURI
2 DATE 1913
2 PLAC Bandera Cemetery, Bandera,															Bandera County,															Texas,																USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 JUN 1913
2 PLAC Bandera, Bandera County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Confederate Army Civil War veteran. TEXSAS STATE TROOPS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezra Alpheus Chipman was the son of Heman and Irene Stoddard Chipman. They lived in Johnstown, Leeds County, Ontario, Canada and moved to the U.S. when Ezra was a small child. Ezra came to Bandera, Texas with the Lyman Wight Mormo
2 CONC n Colony in 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezra married Malinda Porter and they had four children: Heber Nathaniel, Ezra Porter, Amalona who died at the age of 3, and Sanford Porter. Malinda passed away November 17, 1870 in Porterville, Morgan County, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 16, 1847, Ezra married Jeanette Sutherland in Central Texas. They had nine children: Malinda Melissa, Rufana Jane, David Alexander, Robert Alpheus, Irene Marion, Jeanette Armenia, Flora Rosa, Mary Bernice and Ezra Orson. 
2 CONC Jeanette passed away April 8, 1887 in Bandera.
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife was Marion Sutherland, a sister of Jeanette Sutherland. They had two children: Arentha Jane and George Heman. Marion passed away about 1906 and family legend indicates she is buried near Bracketville, Texas in an un
2 CONC marked grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezra died in Bandera June 3, 1913 and is buried in the Bandera Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
