1 NAME Max /Walker/
2 GIVN Max
2 SURN Walker
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 JUN 1926
2 PLAC Brigham
2 ADDR
3 CITY Box Elder
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 DEC 2000
2 PLAC Brigham
2 ADDR
3 CITY Box Elder
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT 1926 ~ 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT Max Walker, 74, loving husband father, grandpa, brother, uncle and friend. Died December 17, 2000. Of heat failure in Brigham, City Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Brigham City on June 20, 1926, a son of Verner and Sylvia Bateman Walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Box Elder High School in 1944 where he participated in school athletics, forging many friendships.
2 CONT
2 CONT Immediately following graduation, he enlisted in the U.S. Navy, was assigned to the U.S.S. Effingham and actively served in the South Pacific conflicts during World War ll.
2 CONT
2 CONT He earned a degree in Accounting from Weber State College, later continuing his education in Business Management at USU and BYU.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Betty Lucille Jones on July 22, 1949, in Brigham City. The marriage was solemnized in September 12, 1956, in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked in the Petroleum Industry for Chevron Oil for 34 years, working in Station Management and as a Sales Representative in Pocatello Id, Brigham City, Salt Lake, Cedar City and Ogden Ut.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1963 he became the Wholesale Distributor for Chevron in Box Elder County, having responsibility for the Tremonton and Brigham City Bulk Plants. He was also employed with the Dunn Oil Co.. and Jardine Petroleum.
2 CONT
2 CONT After retirement, he volunteered as an income tax Advisor for VICA, and was actively engaged in Temple Work and Genealogy. He was a life long member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints and was a High Priest in the B
2 CONC righam City Thirteenth Ward, having previously served at Stake and Ward Financial Clerk, Bishop's Counselor, Stake Young Men's Counselor, Sunday School President, and Home Teacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed sports and was a skilled golfer, winning Club Championships in Tremonton and local tournaments. He especially loved his grandchildren and the special relationship that he had with each one.
2 CONT
