1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...William H. Kimball was a missionary to England 1854-1857. Deputy U.S. marshal three years; sergeant-at-arms in legislature two terms; brigadier-general of Utah militia. Assisted in bringing immigrants to Utah, and went to meet
2 CONC  the Edward Martin "frozen" handcart company. Received reward for discovering the first coal mine within 40 miles of Salt Lake City, known as "Sprague" mine. Postmaster at Parley's Park. Captain of minutemen in early Indian troubl
2 CONC es. Proprietor of Kimball hotel; drove mail and stage line between Salt Lake and Park City between 1870-1885. Second settler in Parley's Park. Died at Coalville, Utah on December 30, 1907...."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': http://www.orsonprattbrown.com/CJB/05Abigail-Smith-Abbott/melissa-burton-coray.html
