1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ann Alice Gheen was born on December 20, 1827 in West Whiteland, Chester Co., Pennsylvania to William Atkins Gheen and Esther Ann Peirce, both of Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann was among the original Mormon Pioneers of 1848 after being baptized on August 15, 1840.  Her endowment was on December 18, 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family Life==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann married Heber Chase Kimball of Vermont, who later became an apostle of the Latter-day Staints, on September 10, 1844 in Nauvoo, Hancock Co., Illinois.  They were sealed on January 7, 1846 in Nauvoo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together, Heber and Ann had six children, all except the first in Salt Lake City:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Samuel H. Kimball, b. 1845 (possibly died young?)
2 CONT * Alice Ann Kimball, b. September 6, 1858 (twin)
2 CONT * Andrew Kimball, b. September 6, 1858 (twin)
2 CONT * Samuel Heber Kimball, b. December 9, 1851
2 CONT * Daniel Heber Kimball, b. February 8, 1856
2 CONT * Sarah Gheen Kimball, b. May 31, 1861
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann died on October 12, 1879 in Salt Lake City, Salt Lake Co., Utah.  She was buried there on October 18.
2 CONT
