1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Kimball, was likewise a most remarkable man. Energetic and zealous always, as an advocate of the restored gospel, he presided over the mission in the Indian Territory for ten years and at intervals returned to Salt Lake to 
2 CONC earn a living for his family. For twenty-six and a half years, from 1898 to the day of his death, he was president of the St. Joseph Stake of Zion, the stake which had been named at the suggestion of President John Taylor in honor
2 CONC  of the Prophet Joseph. His ability as a builder and organizer did much toward the development of a great agricultural empire in eastern Arizona, and in the years of his administration the stake developed from a few wards on the G
2 CONC ila River to some seventeen wards and branches of the church, extending from Miami, Arizona, to El Paso, Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Andrew KIMBALL
