1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Marriage Information==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...42. Adelia Almira Wilcox (Hatton, Wood), born Mar. 29, 1828, Bloomfiled, New York, daughter of Eber and Catherine Noramore Wilcox, died Oct. 19, 1896, Kanosh, Utah. Married and sealed to HCK Oct. 9, 1856, Salt Lake City. No ch
2 CONC ildren by HCK. She married her first husband. William Hawthorne Hatton, May 15, 1844, and bore him three children. One daughter, Mary Eliza Hatton, married Abraham Alonzo Kimball, one of HCK's sons. After Hatton was killed by Indi
2 CONC ans Sept. 13, 1853, at Fillmore, Utah, Adelia became a plural wife of Gideon Durphy Wood on May 25, 1854. There was friction with the first Mrs. Wood, so Adelia got her sealing or marriage canceled Oct. 5, 1856, and went to Salt L
2 CONC ake City, where she eventually married HCK. She was one of the five Utah wives..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: '' Heber C. Kimball: Mormon Patriarch and Pioneer.'' http://books.google.com/books?id=hFRsiNOf_WEC&pg=RA3-PA143&lpg=RA3-PA143&dq=adelia+almira+hatton&source=bl&ots=OdgO70YcbE&sig=kplXZENYx98NLHQlnz3xBFn6BN8&hl=en&ei=iAEuT
2 CONC ZuKIInWtQOdpLj6Aw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&sqi=2&ved=0CBoQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=adelia%20almira%20hatton&f=false
