1 OCCU Conductor of the Mormon Tabernacle Choir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel 1847–1868 [https://history.lds.org/overlandtravels/pioneerDetail?lang=eng&pioneerId=162 Abraham O. Smoot - George B. Wallace Company (1847)]          Age at departure: 39
2 CONT
2 CONT He came with his wife and children. His birth and death dates are confirmed by the Utah State History Cemeteries and Burials Database. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=39124490 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Conductor of the Mormon Tabernacle Choir; 1856-1862.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Oct. 29, 1807 Lancaster, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jun. 21, 1879 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT James is the son of Richard Smithies and Mary Robinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Nancy "Ann" Knowles in the Parish of Milton in the County of York, the Parish of Downham, England on 17 January 1836, by John Wilson, Vicar. In the presence of Robert Smithies and Magdalen Knowles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Hannah Crowther May 2, 1856, Endowment House, Salt Lake Territory, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary ~ Deseret News, Salt Lake City, Utah, Monday, June 23, 1879, Page 3
2 CONT
2 CONT "Funeral Services. ~ The funeral services over the remains of Brother James Smithies, lately deceased, were held today in the school house of Farmer's Ward. A spirited and instructive discourse was delivered by Apostle Jos. F. Smi
2 CONC th. Remarks were made also by Elders A.M. Cannon and D.O. Calder, of the presidency of the Stake, Bishops Sheets and Mousley, and Elders Lorenzo Young and William F. Cahoon, all of whom spoke highly of the integrity and worth of t
2 CONC he deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bro. Smithies was an active member in the Nauvoo brass band, and later acted as leader of the tabernacle choir. He was about seventy two years old, and was universally respected. His remains were brought to the city and interred i
2 CONC n the cemetery."
2 CONT
2 CONT Cause of death was listed as Paralysis. [Source: FHL US/CAN Film (026553), Page 227, A9071] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouses:
