1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary ~ Deseret News, Tuesday, July 13, 1915, Page 11
2 CONT
2 CONT LA BELLE, IDAHO.  DEATH OF A PIONEER OF '47 - (Special Correspondence)
2 CONT
2 CONT La Belle, Jefferson Co., Ida., July 11, - At 12:30 a.m. yesterday Robert Smithies, a pioneer of 1847, died at the residence of his daughter, Mrs. Louisa M. Rosswell (Romwell).  The cause of death was debility and old age. He had b
2 CONC een ailing for three years.  He was the son of James Smithies, and Nancy Knowles, and was born October 5, 1839 in Lancashire, England; came to Utah with his parents in the year 1847, in the month of October.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Scott, April 11, 1865 at Salt Lake City.  She was born March 15, 1847, at what was known as Winter Quarters.  He leaves seven children to mourn his loss, two sons and five daughters.  They are; Mrs. Elizabeth 
2 CONC A. Beck of La Belle, Idaho; Mrs. Sarah M. Bostan (Rostan) of Lorenzo, Idaho; Mrs. Louisa M. Rosswell (Romrell) of La Belle, Idaho;  Alonzo F. Smithies of Lorenzo, Ida.; Isaac W. Smithies of Montpelier, Idaho, Mrs. A. Harrop (Harro
2 CONC t) Walker of Annis, Idaho, and Mrs. Etta Byington of Lava, Idaho.  His wife died 35 years ago, at Salt Lake City, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at LaBelle ward meetinghouse, Tuesday, July 13, at 3 p.m.  Interment will be in the city cemetery, Salt Lake City, Wednesday, July 14.  The remains can be viewed between 10 and 12 a.m., Wednesday the 
2 CONC 14th, at S.M. Taylor & Company's undertaking parlors, No. 251 east First South, Salt Lake City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was a faithful Latter-day Saint, ever ready to perform any task assigned him by those in authority over him.  He held the office of high priest.  He was a kind and loving father, neighbor and friend.  He leaves two brothe
2 CONC rs and six sisters, all residing in different parts of Utah, excepting one sister, Mrs. Sarah E. Scott of Menan, Idaho."
