1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ~ A loving mother, grandmother and sister, Lenore Kimball Farrington, 90, passed away October 23, 1986 of causes incident to age. Born February 22, 1896 in Salt Lake City to Lorenzo H. and Dorothea Soren Christense
2 CONC n or Sorensen, Kimball.  Married Franklin David Farrington, July 17, 1915 in Farmington, Utah; later solemnized in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.  He died Oct 1, 1975.  Member LDS Church.  Worked for the Auerbach Company, and retired a
2 CONC fter many years.  Her family and home were her main interests in life.  (Grandma was a wonderful cook, seamstress and kept her home immaculate.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by children, Donna M. Behm, Franklin D. Jr. (Beverly), John K. (Shirley), Dorothy Hazelgren, Glen D. (Joyce), Kenneth (Judy), all of Salt Lake; Bonnie (Jay) Newman of Seattle, WA.; 46 grandchildren, 96 great-grandchildren
2 CONC , five gg grandchildren, brother, Lorenzo Kimball, Oakland, CA.  Preceded in death by son and daughters; Calthorpe K., Verona Marjorie and Lola G. Rosenlof.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Monday, 1 p.m. Nibley Park Ward, 2450 South 600 East. Friends may call Deseret Mortuary, 36 E. 700 South, Sunday 7-8 p.m. and Monday at the ward one half hour prior to services.  Interment Wasatch Lawn Mem
2 CONC orial Park.
