1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=30042363 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Feb. 22, 1901 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Aug. 14, 1982 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary ~ Salt Lake Tribune, August 15, 1982
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jesse Kimball Burrows, age 81, a gentle man of integrity truly a man without gile, passed away peacefully at home Saturday, August 14, 1982.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born February 22, 1901, Salt Lake City, Utah, a son of Jesse Bullard and Abbie Sarah Kimball Burrows and a grandson of Heber C. Kimball. Married Lydia Fairbanks, Yates, June 20, 1928, in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. Employed by Grani
2 CONC te School District in the purchasing department for 40 years. Former president of Granite Employees' Association; former president of the Heber C. Kimball Family Organization. Always young at heart, he loved his family and life, a
2 CONC nd especially enjoyed traveling, gardening, music, and planning dinners. Active member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, High Priest, completed a Northern States mission in 1924. Ward Clerk, Stake Clerk, bishop's
2 CONC  counselor, stake high councilman. Chairman of the Old Folks Committee which he fondly called the "Young at Heart Committee."
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: wife; nine children, 31 grandchildren; and nine great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Funeral services held Tues. August 17, at the Haven-Kimball Ward, 2280 South 300 East. Friends may call Monday 6-8 p.m. Colonial Mortuary, 2128 South State and at the ward on Tuesday, one hour prior to services." 
2 CONT
