1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (son of John Titcomb and Mary Atkins). Born March 3, 1832, Berkshire, England. Came to Utah October 31, 1849, Ezra T. Benson company.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married:	Lydia Jane Tanner May 26, 1854, Cottonwood, Utah (daughter of John Joshua Tanner and Rebecca Smith of Cottonwood). She was born November 28, 1836.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT             Mary Jane born December 31, 1854, married Thomas Gray;
2 CONT             Joseph Luke born January 10, 1856, married Sarah Larsen;
2 CONT             Rebecca Maria born August 29, 1857, married Thomas Jones;
2 CONT             John Francis born March 1, 1859, died;
2 CONT             Naomi Sophie born February 23, 1863, married Thomas Powers;
2 CONT             Sarah Eunice born July 6, 1864, married Lott Russen;
2 CONT             Helen Elsie born July 11, 1866, married Heber Commer;
2 CONT             Mahonrl born April 6, 1869, married Susan Mower;
2 CONT             Preston Freeman born October 13, 1870;
2 CONT             Lillie Ruth born May 18, 1871, married John Jackson;
2 CONT             Lydia Louisa born February 15, 1873;
2 CONT             Edward Smith born November 30, 1874, died;
2 CONT             Florence May born June 15, 1878, married Alma Berg;
2 CONT             Annie S. born June 14, 1880, died.
2 CONT
2 CONT High Priest; block teacher; Sunday school superintendent. Settled in Lehi 1854. Veteran Indian war. Freighter; shoemaker; farmer. Sources:	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah photographs, page 195
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1215
