3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 NOV 1902
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bryce
3 STAE Arizona
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 JAN 1928
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bountiful
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Reuben Call, who had been very low for nearly two weeks, passed away Friday at her home in Bountiful.  Mrs. Call was the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. William I. Porter, formerly of Centerville, and was born at Bry
2 CONC ce, Arizona, but came to Utah several years ago.  She married Reuben Anson Call July 21, 1926, in the Manti LDS Temple.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, one daughter, Beverly Call, and her father, both of Bountiful, and the following brothers and sisters, Leland and Elbert Porter, Mrs. May Haacke, Miss Areta Porter, and Miss Edna Porter, all of Centervil
2 CONC le, Mrs. Armina Barlow, Bountiful, Mrs. Elizabeth Wood, South Bountiful.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at the Bountiful Tabernacle, Monday, at 1 p. m. D. R. Tolman presided at the services and was one of the speakers. Other speakers were Ira Waite, Bishop Wesley E. Tingey, Harry Simmons and Amos Cook. The
2 CONC re was a good attendance. Interment took place in the Bountiful cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Davis County Clipper January 27, 1928.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
