1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/146263/millie-maria-brown Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 11 2019, 18:10:20 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Evanston, Wyoming -- Mrs. Millie Cornia Porter Brown, 75 of Evanston, died Friday at her home of a heart attack.  Mrs. Brown was born October 23, 1891, in Porterville, Morgan County, Utah, a daughter of Lyman Ozias and Ann Rich Po
2 CONC rter.  She was married to Charles Dean Cornia on September 4, 1912, in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.  He died in 1926 at the age of 38.  They had five children, Elsie, Beulah, Parley, Reta, and Charles O'dell.  Millie had to go to wor
2 CONC k to raise her little family.  She cooked for men on hay camps and on the Monte Cristo Road.  That's where Millie's Spring got its name.  Both Parley and O'dell went to serve their country in World War II.  O'dell, the youngest wa
2 CONC s killed, th only boy from Woodruff.  Millie married William Ezra Brown on May 7, 1938, in Coalville, Utah.  He died June 15, 1962.  She was a member of the LDS Church and was a Gold Star Mother.  She lived in Woodruff, Utah, abou
2 CONC t 20 years, and moved to Almy, Wyoming, and later to Evanston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are one son and three daughters, Parley Cornia, Roosevelt, Utah; Mrs. Arthur (Elsie) Cox, Woodruff;  Mrs. Frank (Beulah) Burleigh, Mrs. Ralph (Rita) McKinnon, both of Evanston;  Robert Borwn, Ogden;  six stepdaughters, M
2 CONC rs. Agnes Carl, Hollywood, California;  Mrs. George (Sarah) Robinson, Evanston;  Mrs. Roy (Bessie) Meadows, Coalville;  Mrs. Ralph (Deloroa) Bateman, Evanston;  Mrs. Les (Eleanor) Wright, Coalville;  Mrs. Carl (Bernice) Warner, Co
2 CONC alville;  43 grandchildren, 34 great-grandchildren, two sisters, Mrs. William (Myrtle) Stromberg, Clearfield;  Mrs. Robert (Lucy) Neilson, Evanston.  Funeral services and burial were to be held today in Woodruff.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
