1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THOMAS J. WHITAKER
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Thomas James Whitaker was born October 14, 1792 in Rotherhithe, Surrey, England to Robert and Ann Whitaker.  He was a customs officer.  He met and feel in love with Mary Ann Betts who lived not far from his home.  Then he left on
2 CONC  a long sea voyage for his boss who was Captain Betts, Mary Ann's father.  He was gone for several years as a business manager in the East Indies.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	He did not know that he had left his young sweetheart pregnant. He was surprised to learn that he had fathered a son.   The couple immediately married upon his return.  They had two more children, both girls.  Mary Ann was quite 
2 CONC frail and died when the youngest girl was just three.  Thomas never remarried.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 	His son Thomas William Whitaker joined the Mormon Church in California.  When he went back to England to visit his father and sisters, he hoped he might convert them.  Yet knowing his stern, unchangeable disposition, he was total
2 CONC ly unprepared for the reception he received.  He tried to talk with is sisters privately, but he was ordered from the house.  His father's parting words were, "When you come to your senses, and renounce Mormonism, you may come bac
2 CONC k to us.  Otherwise, I never want to see your face again."  Thus they parted never to be reunited in this life.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Thoms James died in 1869 in Bermonsdy, England.
