1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles accompanied Rhea on the Tabernacle Choir's European Tour in 1955. They invited Edna, Rhea's sister, and her husband, Had, to join the tour. The Choir traveled extensively through England, dedicating the Lon
2 CONC don Temple and visiting historic places along the way. Charles later said of the impact of the Choir’s concerts: “They would turn the hall on fire!”
2 CONT
2 CONT In Sweden Rhea became friends with their landlady and was convinced the woman was a "Golden Contact." They went throughout Europe visiting friends, seeing museums, going to ‘The Louve’ in France, or going to Switzerland, which was
2 CONC  beautiful. Rhea and Edna wanted to extend their trip visiting Rome, Italy, however Charles and Had needed to return to their homes and jobs. After spending seven more days touring additional museums and churches, Rhea and Edna fl
2 CONC ew home together, stopping in New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT They continued on their flight heading towards Salt Lake City when their United Airlines Flight veered off course toward Medicine Bow Peak in Wyoming where it crashed. All aboard were killed. It was the worst airplane accident in 
2 CONC the history of American aviation up to that time. Charles and the family awaited the news at the airport and crowded into the waiting room when the crash was announced. The family was indeed devastated. Children and grandchildren 
2 CONC who had grown independent on their own suddenly came together to share their grief in this tragedy. Charles and Had were faced with the sad task of informing mother Folsom that she had lost two lovely daughters. It was necessary f
2 CONC or the friends and family to carry on…which they did
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Mrs. Hanks died in the crash of United Air Lines flight 409 at Medicine Bow.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/45353441/edna-hanks
