1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=57357746 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Apr. 26, 1926
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Aug. 18, 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Cresencia Gonzales Cloward, 84, passed away Wednesday, August 18, 2010 surrounded by her family after a courageous 13 year battle with Alzheimer's. She was born April 26, 1926 in Gallina, New Mexico to Amarante and Petreta Chevez 
2 CONC Gonzales. On August 22, 1959, she married Dean L. Cloward in Las Vegas, Nevada. He preceded her in death on December 1, 1998. They resided in Payson moving to Sunset in 1962. Mom and dad enjoyed camping, fishing and hunting with f
2 CONC amily. She enjoyed gardening and sewing. She spent many days quilting. Mom was a hard worker and immaculate housekeeper. She was a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Cresencia is survived by her five childr
2 CONC en: Tony (Jill) Vigil, Mable (Phil) Christensen, Clodie (Carol) Vigil, Tio Vigil, Priscilla (Jay) Offret, a very special niece Lina Gonzales, 10 grandchildren and 11 great-grandchildren. Cresencia was preceded in death by her husb
2 CONC and, Dean, her parents, nine siblings and a very special grandson, Cameron Vigil. Graveside services will be held Saturday, August 21, 2010 at 11 a.m. at the Payson City Cemetery. Services entrusted to Lindquist's Layton Mortuary,
2 CONC  1867 No. Fairfield Road. The family would like to thank a very special person Kathy for care she gave, Chancellor Gardens and Inspiration Hospice. 
2 CONT
