1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Residence''': Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah, United States - 1935
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Ward 1, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake City Precinct, Salt Lake, Utah, United States - 1940
2 CONT * '''Residence''': West Point, Utah - 4 Feb 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Obituary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Geraldine (Jerrie) L. McCafferty,''' 75 passed away Friday, February 4, 2005 at home surrounded by her family and friends. Jerrie was born June 25, 1929 in Salt Lake City, Utah to Arnold R. and Lois V. Terry.
2 CONT She graduated from West High School in SLC. She married David R. McCafferty August 12, 1950 in SLC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jerrie was a housewife and a very loving and caring wife, mother & grandmother. She enjoyed spending time at their second home in Manila, Utah and fishing at Flaming Gorge. She dedicated many hours of volunteer work at LDS Hospita
2 CONC l in SLC, McKay Dee Hospital in Ogden and Davis North Hospital in Layton.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her husband of West Point, Utah; 3 children: Arnold S. (Nancy) McCafferty of Overton, Nevada; Terry R. (Marla) McCafferty of Clinton, and Mitzi (Paul) Larsen of West Point; 9 grandchildren and 4 great-grandchild
2 CONC ren. Also, a very special friend Linda Imboden of S. Ogden who spent countless hours caring for her and a very special CNA Verlynn Miller of Roy.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents Arnold and Lois Terry of SLC; brother, Jack R. Terry of SLC; her twin sons and a great grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to extend their sincere appreciation to Linda Imboden, Marla McCafferty, Vista Care Hospice, especially Marie Jensen, Dan Horton, Verlynn Miller, and Haley Toyn for the special care they provided to our Mothe
2 CONC r during this difficult time. The family would also like to thank the neighbors and friends who visited with her and brought her and her husband lunches.
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside services will be held Tuesday, February 8, 2005 at 2 p.m. at Lindquists Memorial Park Layton, 1867 No. Fairfield Road. Friends and family may call Tuesday from 12:30 to 1:45 p.m. at Lindquists Layton Mortuary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment, Lindquists Memorial Park Layton.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers please make contributions to Vista Care Hospice, 425 E. 5350 S., Suite 155, So. Ogden, Utah 84405 in Memory of Jerrie.
2 CONT
2 CONT E-mail condolences to the family at llm@lindquistmortuary.com.
2 CONT
