1 NAME Lisa Ann /Stone/
2 GIVN Lisa Ann
2 SURN Stone
2 _MARNM Phelps
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 JUL 1956
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 NOV 2025
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/290306646/lisa-ann-phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa Ann Stone Phelps
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 20 Jul 1956
2 CONT Nagoya, Nagoya-shi, Aichi, Japan
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 24 Nov 2025 (aged 69)
2 CONT Saint George, Washington County, Utah, USA
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Mountain View Cemetery
2 CONT Marysvale, Piute County, Utah, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT 290306646
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa Ann Phelps passed away Monday, November 24th 2025 in Saint George Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born July 20th 1956 in Nagoya, Japan to Ambrose Waldo Stone and Leona Marie Giles while her Father was stationed there during his service in the US Air Force. Lisa married James Wallace Phelps on June 14th 1976 in Reno Nev
2 CONC ada and were sealed in the Oakland California LDS temple in August 1977.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa was raised in Japan, Athens Georgia, Bangor Maine, and when her Father retired from the Air Force they moved to the Reno Nevada area where her Father worked at the VA Hospital.
2 CONT While Lisa and James were living in Reno he enlisted in the US Air Force. James was enlisted from 1977 to 1981. During the time James was enlisted Lisa lived in Aurora Colorado then Victorville California (George Air Force Base). 
2 CONC When James was done with his enlistment they moved back to Reno Nevada where he became a truck driver.
2 CONT
2 CONT During their marriage they lived in Reno Nevada, Phoenix Arizona, Salt Lake City Utah, Las Vegas Nevada, and ended up just outside of Mesquite Nevada in Scenic Arizona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa loved her family and was an active member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints where she served in many callings such as Relief Society President, Gospel Doctrine teacher, and most recently as the Music Director
2 CONC  in the Scenic Ward. Lisa loved serving in the Temple and enjoyed the wonderful friendships she made there. Lisa taught herself to play the piano and organ, to paint, sew, quilt, and was a wonderful cook. Lisa and James had just s
2 CONC tarted getting into gardening and she was so excited to see "the fruit of her labors".
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa left High School in 10th grade but went to night school and got her GED. She then went to Business School and received an Associate Degree in Business Management and later became a Certified Nurses Assistant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa is preceded in death by both her parents, Ambrose and Leona (Giles) Stone, both In-Laws Cordell and Jean (Halls) Phelps, older brother Jr. and his wife Debbie, younger brother Harold Stone, and her sister Karen Marshall and h
2 CONC er husband Scott.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisa is survived by her forever companion James Wallace Phelps, 3 children- Daniel (Amanda) Phelps, James (Mindy) Phelps, and Tiffany (Curtis) Harper, 8 grandchildren, 1 great-grand daughter, 1 brother and 4 sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements are under the direction of Spilsbury Mortuary, 110 S Bluff Street, St. George, UT 84770. Funeral services will be Friday, December 5th 2025 at the Littlefield LDS Chapel. located at 3260 Hwy 91, Littlefield, A
2 CONC Z 86432. The viewing will be from 9:30-10:30am MST and Memorial service at 11:00am. Interment will be Monday, December 8th at 1:00pm at the Marysvale Cemetary in Marysvale Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Condolences and memories can be shared online with the family at www.spilsburymortuary.com
