1 NAME Joseph Harris /Ridges/
2 GIVN Joseph Harris
2 SURN Ridges
2 _MARNM Ridges
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 APR 1827
2 ADDR
3 CITY Eling / Marchwood
3 STAE England
1 BAPM
2 DATE 3 AUG 1827
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 MAR 1914
2 PLAC Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah, USA
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 10 MAR 1914
2 PLAC Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Tabernacle organ builder/carpenter
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Harris Ridges, the builder of the Tabernacle organ in Salt Lake City,
2 CONT was born 25 April 1827 in Hampshire, England. He was trained in organ
2 CONT building as a youth in Southampton, England, and built his first organ in
2 CONT Australia, where he was converted to the restored gospel. Having come to
2 CONT the attention of Brigham Young, he moved to Salt Lake City, where he was
2 CONT asked to design an organ suitable for the tabernacle. When the tabernacle
2 CONT was opened for use in 1867, Ridges’ organ was one-third complete. It was
2 CONT finished in 1877 with 2,638 pipes. Through the years, the organ has been
2 CONT rebuilt, electrified, and enlarged to 10,814 pipes. Joseph Ridges died 7
2 CONT March 1914 in Salt Lake City.
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT Encyclopedia of Latter-day Saint History
2 CONT Edited By Arnold K. Garr, Donald Q. Cannon, Richard O. Cowan
2 CONT US/CAN Book 289.309 G191e
2 CONT Page 1030
