1 BURI
2 DATE 13 AUG 1935
2 PLAC Aultorest Cem., Ogden, Weber, UT
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Obituary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT Former Bishop Dies After Short Illness at Home
2 CONT Supervisor of Repairs in Ogden City Schools Succumbs
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogden—'''Wilford Owen Ridges''', 68, former bishop of the Ogden L.D.S. Ninth ward and supervisor of repair work in the Ogden schools for 20 years, died Sunday at the family home, 3162 Adams avenue, of coronary thrombosis. He was s
2 CONC tricken Saturday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Ridges was born September 5, 1866, in Salt Lake City, a son of Joseph H. and Ann Agatha Pratt Ridges, Utah pioneers of 1847. He received his education in Salt Lake City and moved to Ogden in 1891. Mr. Ridges married Letitia Ch
2 CONC ambers in the Salt Lake L.D.S. temple February 26, 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Ridges filled a mission for his church to the southern states from 1892 to 1894, was a member of the Weber stake Sunday school board; of the high council of the Oneida L.D.S. stake, superintendent of Fairview, Idaho, ward Sund
2 CONC ay school, member of the Mount Ogden stake high council, and a counselor in Mount Ogden high priests quorum.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the industrial school board several years and had been manual training instructor at Weber college and at South Washington school.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his widow, seven sons and daughters, Eugene C., Lowell W., J. Harris, John M. and Wilford O. Ridges Jr., Mrs. Milford Piggott and Mrs. Lloyd W. Keller, all of Ogden; five grandchildren and six brothers and sisters: M
2 CONC rs. Clara Bell Pike, Mrs. Louie Carpenter, Mrs. Berniece Haddock and Beatrice Ridges, all of California; Mrs. Florence Dean, Shelley, Idaho, and Joseph P. Ridges, Salt Lake City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements will be announced from the Larkin and Sons mortuary.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: ''Salt Lake Tribune'', Aug. 12, 1935, 7. Retrieved from http://jared.pratt-family.org/parley_family_histories/wilford_ridges_obituary.html
