1 NOTE !SOURCE:  Data for the family of Parley Parker Pratt and Mary Wood is taken
2 CONT from a Family Group Record prepared by the Jared Pratt Family Association,
2 CONT Dorothy G. Topham, President, 423 Seventh Avenue, Salt Lake City, UT 84103,
2 CONT which lists:
2 CONT   - Birth:  Family records of Parley Parker Pratt.  21 leaves.  Manuscript
2 CONT      (handwritten, some holograph).  Photocopy in possession of Jared Pratt
2 CONT      Family Organization (see above), and microfilm copy at Genealogical
2 CONT      Society of Utah, GS Film 430,100; Parley Parker Pratt papers, LDS Church
2 CONT      historical department archives, MS, d, 625; "The Autobiography of Parley
2 CONT      Parker Pratt .../ edited by his son, Parley P. Pratt, Chicago: published
2 CONT      for Pratt Bros. by Law, King & Law, 1888.  502, x p.  See p. x (also in
2 CONT      later editions).
2 CONT   - Wife and marriage data:  Family records of Parley Parker Pratt, GS Film
2 CONT      430,100.
2 CONT   - Death:  Family records of Parley Parker Pratt, GS Film 430,100; "Deseret
2 CONT      News" (12 Nov 1892), p. 2; "Deseret News" (27 Oct 1900); Eleanor McLean
2 CONT      Pratt papers, part of Parley Parker Pratt papers, LDS Church historical
2 CONT      department archives, MS, d, 625; George Higginson, "Account of the
2 CONT      assassination of Parley P. Pratt," manuscript (holograph), part of Parley
2 CONT      Parker Pratt papers, LDS Church historical department archives, MS, d,
2 CONT      625; Steven Pratt, "Eleanor McLean and the murder of Parley P. Pratt,"
2 CONT      Brigham Young University Studies, 15 (Winter 1975), 225-256.  See p. 246.
2 CONT   - Burial:  Eleanor McLean Pratt papers and George Higginson, "History of the
2 CONT      Cherokee Mission," manuscript (holograph), both part of Parley Parker
2 CONT      Pratt papers, LDS Church historical department archives, MS, d, 625.
2 CONT NOTE-SRE-Mum's info says that this cemeter in Richmond, MO.
2 CONT   - Parents:  Family records of Parley Parker Pratt, GS Film 430,100; "The
2 CONT      Autobiography of Parley Parker Pratt, p. x; Orson Pratt's own manuscript
2 CONT      record (in back portion of F. W. Chapman's "The Pratt Family: or the
2 CONT      Descendants of Lieutenant William Pratt ..." -- Hartford, Conn.:  Case,
2 CONT      Lockwood, 1864 (GS Film 599,765).
2 CONT   - Wife's death:  "Deseret News" (5 Mar 1898).
2 CONT   - Wife's burial:  Sexton's records, City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~  - Baptism:  "Parley P. Pratt, Baptised, Confirmed and Ordained an Elder of  the Church of Jesus Christ of LatterDay [sic] saints On, or abought [sic]  the first day of September A.D. 1830 By the hand of Oliver Cowdery, at the  
2 CONC house of Jacob Whitmer, Near Waterloo, Seneca Co., N.Y.  The Baptism being  performed in Seneca Lake."  "Parley P. Pratt, renewed his covenant before  the Lord an [sic] was Baptised and Confirmed anew in the Gift of the Holy  Ghos
2 CONC t, and in all his blessings, Covenants, promises, Ordainations [sic],  Washings, Anointings, Sealings, Priesthood, Apostleship, and the powers  thereof by the Hands of President John Taylor, at the City of Great Salt Lake on the 2
2 CONC 8th of November A.D. 1847."  Family records of Parley Parker Pratt, leaves 1, 5 (GS Film 430,100). - Endowment:  Joseph Smith, "Documentary History of the Church," VI, 98; TIB;  Nauvoo Temple, 1845-1846, Endowments for the Living,
2 CONC  GS Film 183,393.
2 CONT
2 CONT ! - Misc.:  TIB; GS Archives; GS Patrons (four-generation) sheets; etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT !SOURCE:  Also from a Family Record kept by Helaman Pratt, in possession of Mrs.
2 CONT Emaline P. Bluth, 782 West Maple, Mapleton, UT 84663.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NOTE:  Parley Parker Pratt was an Apostle of Jesus Christ, Utah Pioneer,
2 CONT Legislator, teacher, farmer, author, poet, statesman, explorer, road builder,
2 CONT missionary, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~NOTE:  On the Jared Pratt Family Group Sheet, endowment date for Parley Parker
2 CONT Pratt is given as 10 Dec 1845 NV.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NOTE:  Information on other wives found "Pratt Pioneers of Utah" by Arthur D.
2 CONT Coleman.
