2 CONT Obituary ~ Deseret News, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah, Friday, December 7, 1956, Page B17, Col. 6
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mrs. Josephine Brinton Driggs, 76, 2048 E. 4800 South, Holladay, died 9 p.m. Wednesday in a Salt Lake hospital after a lingering illness.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Jan 18, 1880, to Joseph Hammond and Mary Howard Brinton, in Holladay.  Married Mark Kimball Driggs May 10, 1898.  He died Sept. 21, 1940.  Member of Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: two sons, Vaughn B., Chase, Salt Lake City; three dauhters, Mrs. Mary D. Hubbard, Salt Lake City; Mrs. June Smith, Mrs. Madeline Waddoups, San Francisco; 13 grandchildren, 13 great grandchildren, three brothers and thre
2 CONC e sisters.  Funeral arrangements will be announced from 260 E. South Temple."
2 CONT
2 CONT Deseret News, Saturday, December 8, 1956, Page B5, Col. 5 "Funeral services for Josephine Brinton Driggs will be held Monday at 1 p.m. in the Holladay 1st Ward chapel, 2241 E. 4800 South.  Friends may call at the Larkin Mortuary, 
2 CONC 260 E. South Temple Sunday from 5 to 7 p.m. and Monday 1 hr. prior to services at the Ward.  Interment in the Holladay Cemetery.  Funeral directors, Larkin Mortuary."* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30080808/josep
