1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Glenn Dean Farrington passed away on October 10, 2008 of complications due to Leukemia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on February 21, 1929 in Salt Lake City. Glenn attended West High, served in the National Guard for eight years. Later drafted into the Army/Air force 653 field artillery during the Korean Conflict. He was a Disabled Am
2 CONC erican Veteran. Married Joyce Jackson in Salt Lake City on February 18, 1950. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a skilled craftsman, worked 39 years for the Amoco refinery. He was passionate about golf, bowling, traveling and exploring new sites. He enjoyed spending winters in Yuma, AZ, and summers at the El Nautica boat club. He had
2 CONC  a great love for people and would do anything to help anyone in need, especially his family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by his loving wife, Joyce, four sons and two daughters: Glenn Dean Jr. (Lynn), Jeffrey, Michael (Denise), Cindy (Judd) Larson, AZ, Lori (Tony) Wright, Coalville, Rodney (Lisa), 38 grandchildren and 14 great-grandchildren 
2 CONC Also survived by his brother John, (Shirley) SLC; sisters: Dorothy (Rudy) Nolty, Sandy; and Bonnie Newman SLC; Kenneth (Judy) SLC; sister-in-law, Beverly, SLC. Preceded in death by his brothers Cal, Bud, sisters Donna, Lola and Ma
2 CONC rjorie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services will be held on Tuesday, October 14, 2008 at 11 a.m. at the Winder West Stake Center, 4551 South 1200 East. A viewing will be held on Monday, October 13th from 6-8 p.m. and from 10-11 a.m. on the 14th at the Winde
2 CONC r West Stake Center.  Interment: Mountain View Memorial Estates Cemetery, 3115 East Bengal Boulevard (7800 South).   Published in the Deseret News from 10/12 and 10/13/2008.
