1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edward is the son of William Wendel and Mary Ellen Myers, Weber.  On April 21, 1910, he married Lucile Margaret Skinner at Hyde Park Chapel in Chicago, Cook Co., IL.  Lucile died in 1947.  Edward married Verna Kimb
2 CONC all, Archer on July 17, 1949, in Salt Lake City, Utah, where he was a resident for sixteen years. Verna was born May 3, 1892, Salt Lake City, Utah and died January 11 1984 in Salt lake City, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ed was vice president of the American Sugar Refining Co., where he had been employed since 1917.  He was elected as vice president in 1926 and retired in 1947. He began his caraeer in law in 1899, after attending the Wittenberg Ac
2 CONC ademy and Wittenberg College in Springfield, Ohio.  He served as a student of law under Thomas R. Marshall, later vice president of the United States.   Ed was purchasing agent for Booth Fisheries Co., Chicago, and was enlisted in
2 CONC  the 3rd Ohio Volunteer Infantry during the Spanish-American War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ed and Lucile are the parents of three children; John S.,  Rochester, N.Y., Mrs. Leon J. (Margaret) Didion, Salt Lake City; Mrs. Alfred (Carolyn) Schlesinger, Armonk, N.Y., and ten grandchildren.  Survivors; sisters, Jessie Elizab
2 CONC eth (Homer LeMar) Kitt, Ruth Christina (Thomas O. Miller) and Mrs. Weber Armstrong, all of Washington, D. C. Services were Friday in White Plains, New York.
