1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=30043127 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 5, 1907 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jun. 20, 1997 Sandy Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary ~ Deseret News, Sunday, June 22, 1997, Page B6
2 CONT
2 CONT "Lydia Fairbanks Yates Burrows ~ On the 69th Anniversary of their wedding day, Lydia and Jesse were united once again! This joyous reunion took place June 20, 1997 as Lydia Fairbanks Yates Burrows returned to Heaven and joined her
2 CONC  beloved husband, Jesse Kimball Burrows, who preceded her in death 15 years ago (Aug 14, 1982).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia was born in Salt Lake City, Utah on June 5, 1907 to Thomas Jarvis Yates and Lillie Annetta Fairbanks Yates. She recently celebrated her 90th birthday.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was raised with nine siblings; Leah, Vera, Alton, Huish, Erma, Lilly, Cora, Lora, and Glen. All preceded her in death. Survived by one sister-in-law, Alta Yates.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our mother loved her home, music, making quilts, cooking, traveling, reunions, gardening, entertaining, collecting pioneer heirlooms and writing family histories. Lydia made many close friends while serving in Primary, Sunday Scho
2 CONC ol, Relief Society, as a visiting teacher, in the Daughters of the Utah Pioneers and helping handicapped children. She was the Utah Mother of the year in 1983. Lydia is an unselfish friend and neighbor. Her Heavenly Father, the Sa
2 CONC vior, the scriptures and her family are her greatest loves. The world is a better place because of her life. Survivors; nine children, 32 grandchildren, 71 great grandchildren and four gg grandchildren. Preceded in death by husban
2 CONC d, a grandson and a great-grandson. A special thanks to Dr. Robert C. Hill and Vista Hospice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Wednesday, June 25, 1997 in the Sandy 13th Ward chapel, 586 Est 8400 South. Friends may call at Wasatch Lawn Mortuary, 3401 South Highland Drive on Tuesday from 6 to 8:30 p.m. and at the Wa
2 CONC rd Chapel Wednesday from 9:45 to 10:45 a.m. prior to services. Interment, Salt Lake City Cemetery."
2 CONT
