1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=93391912 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 15, 1950 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jul. 7, 2012 Murray Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Our beloved sister, aunt and friend Becky Burrows, 62, passed away at her home in Murray, UT, on July 7, 2012. We can only imagine the wonderful reunion taking place in heaven! Becky began her earthly journey on June 15, 1950 in S
2 CONC alt Lake City. She was the youngest of nine children born to devoted parents Lydia Fairbanks Yates and Jesse Kimball Burrows. Becky loved cutting, gluing and coloring her "papers". She was organized and knew where everything belon
2 CONC ged. Puzzles, movies and celebrating her birthday and Christmas would bring her such joy. Becky loved to go for a hamburger and root beer. She was so graceful and had good rhythm when she danced with Anne Riordan's Sunrise Dance G
2 CONC roup. Many of the schools Becky attended were co-founded by her mother including a Special Primary at Forrest Dale Ward. Becky competed in the Special Olympics. At her request Becky was baptized on June 4, 1988 and enjoyed proxy b
2 CONC aptisms at the Jordan River Temple. She attended Special Needs Mutual, received her patriarchal blessing and enjoyed handing out programs in the Sandy 13th Ward. Becky loved music and would sing with her hands. She enjoyed being a
2 CONC  member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints. Having many health issues Becky was so brave and we learned many things from her. After the death of her parents she was lovingly cared for by her sister, Mary Robison. T
2 CONC he whole Robison family helped with Becky, including "daddy" John and her best friend, Kalyn. No one was given more love than Becky! The family would like to thank the staff of Harmony Home Hospice, Vicky, Crystal and Laura, for t
2 CONC heir loving attention. Survivors include siblings: Leah (Jesse) Poulson, Roy Spjut, Marvin (Shirla) Burrows, Naomi (Lynn) Foote, Nancy Wright, Mary (John) Robison & Frances Nelson and many nieces and nephews. Preceded in death by 
2 CONC her parents, sisters, Abbie Spjut & Annette Church, and brother-in-law, Edward Wright. Funeral services will be held at 11:00 am on Thursday, July 12, 2012 at the Murray 16th Ward 610 West 5750 South, Murray, UT where friends and 
2 CONC family may call from 9:30-10:45am prior to services. Interment at Salt Lake City Cemetery under the direction of Wasatch Lawn Mortuary. Condolences may be shared at www.wasatchlawn.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
