1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Rulon Seymour Wells''' (July 7, 1854 – May 7, 1941) was a Utah politician and was a general authority of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church) from 1893 until his death..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Wells was born in Salt Lake City, Utah Territory to LDS Church leader Daniel H. Wells (1814–1891) and Louisa Free (1824–1886). In 1875, Wells travelled to Europe as a Mormon missionary and worked primarily in Germany and Switz
2 CONC erland. He returned to the United States in 1877. On January 18, 1883 he married Josephine Eliza Beatie (1857–1923).
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1893, Wells was chosen as a member of the seven-man First Council of the Seventy. In 1896, he succeeded Anthon H. Lund as the president of the European Mission of the church, headquartered in Liverpool, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT In December 1898, Wells returned to Utah. In the United States election in 1900, Wells was elected to the Utah House of Representatives. He served as a member of the house for its 4th session, which lasted from January to March 19
2 CONC 01. He did not stand for re-election in 1902.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of J. Golden Kimball in 1938, Wells became the senior president of the Seventy, a position he held until his own death in 1941.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wells died in Salt Lake City from colon cancer; he had been a general authority of the church for almost 50 years..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'':  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rulon_S._Wells
