1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Junius Free Wells (June 1, 1854 – April 15, 1930[1]) was the first head of the Young Men's Mutual Improvement Association, an organization which is today the Young Men organization of The Church of Jesus Christ of 
2 CONC Latter-day Saints (LDS Church). He also was a magazine founder, an author, and the chief organizer of the LDS Church's efforts to build a number of historical monuments in the early 1900s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Salt Lake City, Utah Territory, Wells was the son of LDS Church leader Daniel H. Wells and his fourth wife, Hannah Corrilla Free.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junius_F._Wells
