1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (son of Warren Smith and Amanda Barnes of Marion, Ohio). Born December 16, 1833, at, Marion. Came to Utah 1848, Joseph Young company.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married:	Telitha Free March 1855, Salt Lake City (daughter of Absalom Free and Betsy Strait of St. Clair county, Illinois, pioneers 1848, Joseph Young company). She was born October 5, 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT             Alma L., married Marguerite Black, married Annie Roberts;
2 CONT             Willard P., married Cora A. Fisher;
2 CONT             Hammer, died aged 2;
2 CONT             Florence, died aged 4;
2 CONT             Cora, married John Hodson;
2 CONT             Rosa, died child;
2 CONT             Julian F., married Pearl Colton;
2 CONT             Betsy, died aged 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Family home Salt Lake City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Missionary to England two years; to Sandwich Islands ten years; high priest; bishop of Coalville three years; high councilor of Summit stake. County recorder Summit county six years. Bookkeeper; contractor. Died June 1887 at Coalv
2 CONC ille, Utah. Sources:	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah photographs, page 171
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1171
2 CONT
