1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Isaac Warriner''', son of Benjamin Warriner and Mercy Bartlett, was born 28 August 1745 in Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lydia Fury, of Wilbraham, Hampden County, in 1767; banns were recorded 11 April 1767. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jacob, b. 18 April 1768 in Wilbraham
2 CONT # Sarah, b. 13 August 1769 in Wilbraham; d. 20 January 1770 in Wilbraham
2 CONT # Sarah, or "Sally", b. 10 July 1771 in Wilbraham; m. Joseph Hatfield 1771 in Springfield
2 CONT # Rach(a)el, b. prob. 1774 in Ludlow, Hampden County; d. 4 September 1844 in her 70th year; did not marry
2 CONT # Chloe, b. prob. in Ludlow; m. John Collins 1799, "both of Springfield"
2 CONT # Justin, b. 27 April 1783 in Springfield
2 CONT # Isaac, b. 14 October 1788 in Springfield; d. 7 January 1803 in Springfield, in his 15th year
2 CONT
2 CONT The family lived in Ludlow for some time after 1771; Isaac and brother Israel appeared at a town meeting there in March 1774 and were elected to office.
2 CONT
2 CONT He made his will 11 March 1803 and bequeathed to his wife, Lydia, his entire estate, real and personal. Nevertheless small sums were given to his two sons, Jacob and Justin, and to his daughters, namely Sally, wife of Joseph Hatfi
2 CONC eld; Rachael Warriner; and Chloe, wife of John Collins. His wife refused to execute the trust as executrix, and the court appointed Edward Pynchon administrator. Amount to be divided among creditors was $145.93.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac died on 14 March 1803, three days after making his will. Lydia, his widow, died on 25 July 1815, in her 72nd year.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' Will dated 11 March 1803. Probated 4 October 1803. Records are in Hampshire County collection despite the family not living there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
