2 CONT Profile last modified 23 Dec 2023 | Created 8 Jun 2014
2 CONT Francis Colegrove Jr. (1698 - 1746)
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Colegrove Jr.
2 CONT Born 20 Aug 1698 in Westerly, Kings, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT Son of Francis Colgrove Sr. and Anna Hannah (Unknown) Colegrove
2 CONT Brother of Eleazear Colegrove, Stephen (Colgrove) Colegrove Sr., John Colegrove Esq. and Ellizabeth (Colegrove) Williams [half]
2 CONT Husband of Welthian (Taylor) Colegrove — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Bailey) Colgrove — married 5 Mar 1718 in Westerly, Kings, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Elizabeth (Colegrove) Tanner, William Colegrove and Jeremiah Colegrove
2 CONT Died 1746 at about age 47 in Tioga, Tioga County, Pennsylvania, USAmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Kevin McClain private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 13 Jan 2024 | Created 8 Jun 2014
2 CONT This page has been accessed 596 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Colegrove was born on 20 August 1698 in Westerly, Kent, Rhode Island to Francis Colegrove and Ann ________, both of Wales. He died in 1746 in Tioga, Tioga, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT The book History and Genealogy of the Colegrove Family in America does not name the wife of Francis but lists 2 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel
2 CONT
2 CONT There is speculation that Francis Colegrove, Sr. may have married Hannah Bailey. Richard Bailey of Newport, Rhode Island, and Samuel Bailey of Westerly, Rhode Island: Father and Son, states because if the dates and deed (Westerly 
2 CONC Deeds, 3:32), that Samuel Bailey conveyed to his (son-in-law-) Francis Colegrove, Jr. and his wife Hannah Colegrove, thirty acres in Westerly, that Francis Colegrove, Jr. is Hannah's husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Death place of Tioga Center, Tioga, New York, United States did not exist in the year of his death, 1746. Tioga County Pennsylvania was formed on 1804. The Find A Grave source has the Tioga Pennsylvania location.
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Colegrove, William, History and Genealogy of the Colegrove Family in America; with biographical sketches, portraits, etc. Chicago, 1894. https://archive.org/details/historygenealogy00cole/page/24?q=Francis+Colegrove
2 CONT Brown, Henrietta Brady. Some Venables of England and America and Brief Accounts of Families Into Which Certain Venables Married. Cincinnati, Kinderton Press. 1961. page 336. https://archive.org/details/somevenablesofen00brow/page/
2 CONC 336?q=Rhode+Island%2C+Vital+Extracts+colegrove
2 CONT Swanson, Scott G, Richard Bailey of Newport, Rhode Island, and Samuel Bailey of Westerly, Rhode Island: Father and Son, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, (July 2014) Vol. 168, Page 195
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/187536673/francis-colegrove findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
