2 CONT Hannah (Bailey) Colgrove (abt. 1700 - aft. 1737)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Colgrove formerly Bailey
2 CONT Born about 1700 in Newport, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Daughter of Samuel Bailey Sr and Elizabeth (Rogers) Bailey
2 CONT Sister of Richard Bailey, Elizabeth Bailey, Jeremiah C Bailey Sr., Samuel Bailey and Judith (Bailey) Warren
2 CONT Wife of Francis Colegrove Jr. — married 5 Mar 1718 in Westerly, Kings, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Mother of Ellizabeth (Colegrove) Williams, Elizabeth (Colegrove) Tanner, William Colegrove and Jeremiah Colegrove
2 CONT Died after 1737 after about age 37 in Hopkinton, Washington, Rhode Islandmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Stephen Sanders private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 23 Jun 2022 | Created 6 Oct 2017
2 CONT This page has been accessed 456 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was born in 1700 in Newport, RI to Samuel Bailey and Elizabeth Rogers. She passed away in 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is speculation that Francis, the father, may have married Hannah Bailey. Richard Bailey of Newport, Rhode Island, and Samuel Bailey of Westerly, Rhode Island: Father and Son, states because if the dates and deed (Westerly De
2 CONC eds, 3:32), that Samuel Bailey conveyed to his (son-in-law-) Francis Colegrove, Jr. and his wife Hannah Colegrove, thirty acres in Westerly, that Francis Colegrove, Jr. is Hannah's husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT The Narragansett historical register, a magazine devoted to the antiquities, genealogy and historical matter illustrating the history of the state of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations . Providence, R.I., The Narragansett His
2 CONC torical Publishing Company. 1882. pg 51. https://archive.org/details/narragansetthist01prov/page/50
2 CONT Swanson, Scott G. Richard Bailey of Newport, Rhode Island, and Samuel Bailey of Westerly, Rhode Island: Father and Son The New England Historical and Genealogical Register (July 2014) Vol. 168, Page 194-195
