2 CONT
2 CONT  The Mayflower.
2 CONT William West was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT Join: Mayflower Project
2 CONT Discuss: MAYFLOWER
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William West, son of Francis West and Susanna (Soule) West, and grandson of Mayflower immigrant George Soule, was born in what is now North Kingstown, Rhode Island, New England, on 31 May 1681.[1] In 1681, North Kingstown and Sout
2 CONC h Kingstown were still one town and there were no counties in Rhode Island at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abiah Sprague married William West of Kingston, "m. (pub. Dec. 24, 1709)'" in Hingham, Massachusetts, [2][3] although the Mayflower Families in Progress "Soule" book just says about 1707, perhaps in Providence, Rhode Island. Abiah
2 CONC  died before 7 April 1721, when her father William wrote his will, naming her children Deborah, William, John, and Abiah West.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William married again, this time, about 1722, to Jane Tanner, who was the daughter of Francis and Mary (Babcock) Tanner. Jane m. (2) in 1751 John Hill.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William West of Kingstown, husbandman, and his first wife Abiah sold land in Kingstowne to John Crowder, weaver, in Aug. 1711. They sold 33 acres in Kingstown, on [2]8 April 1713, to Robert Renalds.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 July 1741, "William West, wife and children" were to be transported from Charlestown, Rhode Island, to North Kingstown, by order of the Charlestown Town Council. And in July 1742, he and some of the family were living in West G
2 CONC reenwich with Benjamin Tanner, when the town council of there asked for an explanation.[1] There was also a William West on the 19 Jan 1744 rate bill for South Kingstown, Rhode Island, but it is unknown if this is the correct Will
2 CONC iam.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate records for William have not been found, but we know he was alive in July 1742 and that Jane remarried in 1751, making his death between July 1742 and 1751.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Samuel West's Memorandum Book : "My grandfathers name was William West his sons names ware William John Joseph BenjaminThomas Francis Hezekiah and Ebenezar his daugthters names ware Deborah Abiah Jane & Susanna."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah, daughter of Abiah, born about 1708; died after 11 Nov 1723
2 CONT William, son of Abiah, born c. 1710 (based on his age at death)
2 CONT John, son of Abiah, born 25 Nov 1715,
2 CONT Abiah, daughter of Abiah, born c. 1718 and before 1 April 1721 (will of grandfather)
2 CONT Child??? West, of Abiah, b. c. 1720; died young before 1 April 1721??
2 CONT Child??? West of Jane, b. c. 1723; died young???
2 CONT Joseph, son of Jane, born about 1724, based on his age at death
2 CONT Jane, daughter of Jane, born about 1726
2 CONT Susanna, daughter of Jane, born about 1728
2 CONT Benjamin, son of Jane, born about 1730
2 CONT Thomas, son of Jane, born about 1732 based on his age at death
2 CONT Francis, son of Jane, born about about 5 Aug. 1735 based on his age at death
2 CONT Hezekiah, son of Jane, b. about 1737; no further record
2 CONT Ebenezer, son of Jane, born probably before 1739
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6 1.7 1.8 George Soule of the Mayflower and his Descendants for Four Generations. Originally compiled by John E. Soule and Milton E. Terry. Revised by Louise Walsh Throop. Mayflower Families in Progress
2 CONC . Seventh Edition. Plymouth: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2015.
2 CONT ↑ History of the Town of Hingham, Massachusetts: Volume 3. Genealogical published by the town 1893.p. 165
2 CONT ↑ Ancestry.com. Massachusetts, Town and Vital Records, 1620-1988 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2011. Original data: Town and City Clerks of Massachusetts. Massachusetts Vital and Town Records. 
2 CONC Provo, UT: Holbrook Research Institute (Jay and Delene Holbrook). Link at Ancestry ($) lines 13 & 14 a marriage intention "propose"
2 CONT Sprague, Frank William. The Brothers Ralph and William Sprague and Some of Their Descendants, The New England Historical & Genealogical Register (NEHGS, Boston, Mass., 1909) Vol. 63, Page 149
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/william-west-24-28kg47v
2 CONT
2 CONT William West (1681 - 1742)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Kingston, Washington, Rhode Island, USA on 31 May 1681 to Francis West and Sarah Hilliard. William West passed away on 1742 in Westerly, Washington, Rhode Island, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT William West family tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis West 1662 - 1724
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in North Kingstown, Washington, Rhode Island, USA in 1662 ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Hilliard Unknown - Unknown
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT It does appear to be the case that William had two wives, the first of whom died after the birth of 4 known children. I have attached the marriage record of William West and Abiah Sprague from 1709 under Sources. Although none of 
2 CONC William and Abiah's children seem to have any birth or christening records, Abiah is mentioned in two Rhode Island land deeds with her husband William. William and Abiah's children are also mentioned in Abiah's father's will. Her 
2 CONC father’s will dated 7 April 1721, probated in Providence RI, 11 Nov. 1723 named Deborah, John, William and Abiah West as his grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the above-referenced journal entry of Samuel West, William had many more children, and apparently at least one more wife - Jane Tanner. None of these children seem to have any birth or christening records either, but 
2 CONC people have generally subtracted out Abiah's children from the list given by Samuel West of William West's children, and then kind of lumped the rest as belonging to Jane Tanner. Apparently Abiah died before her father's will was 
2 CONC written in 1721, and since there is no marriage record between a William West and a Jane Tanner, have assumed the marriage date to be sometime around the writing of Abiah's father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 July 1741 the Charlestown RI Town Council ordered "William West, wife and children" be transported to No. Kingstown. William and some of his family were in W. Greenwich as guests of Benjamin Tanner when the Town Council aske
2 CONC d Benjamin Tanner for an explanation. Apparently they were not welcome - some towns were
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis West and his wife Susannah had several children while living in "Kings Towne," some of whom have actual birth records. On ancestry.com you can find the collection, "Rhode Island, Vital Extracts, 1636-1899 Vol. 05: Washingt
2 CONC on County: Births, Marriages, Deaths," which is an indexed copy of some original records. In this collection, there is a birth record for William of Francis & Susannah West, May 31, 1681, and one for Thomas of Francis & Susannah W
2 CONC est, September 18, 1684. Next to this there is a strange appendage: "I have Clement, instead of Thomas, at same date, R.G.H." Some have suggested that perhaps Clement and Thomas were twins. I don't know. A birth record for William
2 CONC  is attached under Sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT The identification of William's mother as Susannah maiden name Soule comes from an article published in 1924 in The Mayflower Descendant (volume 26 No. 1 starting on page 1). I couldn't find this volume online, so I have scanned t
2 CONC he most relevant pages in under the Memories tab. The article was written by George Ernest Bowman about a "Memmorandum Book" written by Elder Samuel West. Much of the book appears to be written around 1800 and in said book Elder S
2 CONC amuel West wrote: "my great grandfather Francis West Came from Europe to Amarica [sic] Soon after the first Settlement at Plymouth and Soon after his arival [sic] he married A young Lady By the name of Sole daughter of Mr George S
2 CONC ole (he came with his family to Plymouth in the first Vessel that Came their [sic] from Europe) by whoom [sic] he had Seven Sons & 2 daughters his Sons names ware [sic] Francis Thomas Peter William Richard Clemment & John his daug
2 CONC hters names ware [sic] Martha & Susanna martha married a Fones by whoom [sic] She had Children Susanna married a Barber By whoom She had a number of Sons & daughters"
2 CONT Since there is no way to really double-check this information with any primary sources, it has generally been accepted by genealogists.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since the above-referenced Samuel West was a descendant of Francis through this William West, the next sentence of his Memmorandum Book is also relevant: "My grandfathers name was William West his Sons names ware William John Jose
2 CONC ph Benjamin Thomas Francis Hezekiah and Ebenezar his daughters names ware Deborah Abiah Jane & Susanna My fathers mother was Jane Tanner Daughter of Francis Tanner hur mother was a Babcock hur Brothers names ware William Benjamin 
2 CONC John Francis & Nathan hur sisters names ware Mary Avis Abigail Rechel Ann & Dorcas"
2 CONT
2 CONT So apparently William had the following sons:
2 CONT William
2 CONT John
2 CONT Joseph
2 CONT Benjamin
2 CONT Thomas
2 CONT Francis
2 CONT Hezekiah
2 CONT Ebenezer
2 CONT
2 CONT and the following daughters:
2 CONT Deborah
2 CONT Abiah
2 CONT Jane
2 CONT Susanna
2 CONT for a total of 12 children with two wives.
2 CONT
2 CONT It does appear to be the case that William had two wives, the first of whom died after the birth of 4 known children. I have attached the marriage record of William West and Abiah Sprague from 1709 under Sources. Although none of 
2 CONC William and Abiah's children seem to have any birth or christening records, Abiah is mentioned in two Rhode Island land deeds with her husband William. William and Abiah's children are also mentioned in Abiah's father's will. Her 
2 CONC father’s will dated 7 April 1721, probated in Providence RI, 11 Nov. 1723 named Deborah, John, William and Abiah West as his grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the above-referenced journal entry of Samuel West, William had many more children, and apparently at least one more wife - Jane Tanner. None of these children seem to have any birth or christening records either, but 
2 CONC people have generally subtracted out Abiah's children from the list given by Samuel West of William West's children, and then kind of lumped the rest as belonging to Jane Tanner. Apparently Abiah died before her father's will was 
2 CONC written in 1721, and since there is no marriage record between a William West and a Jane Tanner, have assumed the marriage date to be sometime around the writing of Abiah's father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 July 1741 the Charlestown RI Town Council ordered "William West, wife and children" be transported to No. Kingstown. William and some of his family were in W. Greenwich as guests of Benjamin Tanner when the Town Council aske
2 CONC d Benjamin Tanner for an explanation. Apparently they were not welcome - some towns were 
