2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Tanner, wife of William West, and apparently daughter of William and Mary (Babcock) Tanner, was born in Westerly, Rhode Island, about 1702. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the second wife of William West married about 1722. 27 July 1741, the Town Council of Charlestown, Rhode Island ordered "William West wife and childre" be transported to No. Kingstown. William and some family members were 
2 CONC in West Greenwich as guests of Benjamin Tanner by July 1742, then that town council asked Tanner for an explanation. A William West was taxed (rates) 19 Jan 1744 for South Kingstown.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT After William's death, Jane married at Richmond, Rhode Island in 1751 John Hill, born at Westerly , Rhode Island 3 Oct 169[9], son of John and Mary Hill. John and his first wife, Mercy, had about 10 children. About 1737/8 he remov
2 CONC ed to Stonington, Connecticut, and then to Southern Precinct, Dutchess Co., New York, paying taxes there 1747-1756.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hill and his wife Mercy joined the Westerly Sabbatarian Church 1740-50 as did William and Mary West. In 1747, a John Hill was listed in Charlestown , Rhode Island. John Hill of Westerly, Rhode Island, and his wife Jane Hill s
2 CONC old 12.75 acres of land 3 Sept 1756. On 31 Jan 1758 John Hill of Hopkinton, Rhode Island, cordwinder, and Jane Hill his wife sold 30 acres to Joshua Lanphear, of Hopkinton. In July 1768 John Hill, of "Oblong, New York", was in the
2 CONC  Hopkinton, Rhode Island, Sabbatarian Church records.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Hill died perhaps in Dutchess Co., New York after 31 Jan 1758 (deed) died after 27 July 1741 and perhaps by July 1742.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Samuel West's Memorandum Book:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "My grandfathers name was William West his sons names ware William John Joseph Benjamin Thomas Francis Hezekiah and Ebenezar his daughters names ware Deborah Abiah Jane & Susanna. "My fathers mother was Jane Tanner Daughter of Fra
2 CONC nces Tanner hur mother was a Babcock hur Brothers names ware William Benjamin John Frances & Nathan hur sisters names ware Mary Avis Abigail Rechel Ann & Dorcas."
2 CONT William West's siblings were exactly as Samuel named them. However there isn't a Francis Tanner available to be the grandfather of Samuel as asserted in his "Memorandum" above. Rather it was William Tanner and his wife Mary Babcoc
2 CONC k who who were the parents of: William, Benjamin, John, and Jane. William Tanner was also the father of: Francis, Nathan, Mary, Avis, Abigail, Anna, Rebecca and Elizabeth by his third wife Elizabeth. Samuel West's Memorandum which
2 CONC  includes daughters Jane, Rachel, and Dorcas is unique to his account of the Tanner family members, the Tanner Genealogy by George Tanner does not include these three children. There is however other supporting material connecting
2 CONC  Jane as daughter, but not Rachel and Dorcas, consequently these two may or may not be children of William Tanner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Jane[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child??? West of Jane, b. c. 1723; died young???
2 CONT Joseph, son of Jane, born about 1724, based on his age at death
2 CONT Jane, daughter of Jane, born about 1726
2 CONT Susanna, daughter of Jane, born about 1728
2 CONT Benjamin, son of Jane, born about 1730
2 CONT Thomas, son of Jane, born about 1732 based on his age at death
2 CONT Francis, son of Jane, born about about 5 Aug. 1735 based on his age at death
2 CONT Hezekiah, son of Jane, b. about 1737; no further record
2 CONT Ebenezer, son of Jane, born probably before 1739
2 CONT
