1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Descendant of Mayflower passenger George Soule
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin West, son of William West and his second wife Jane Tanner, was born about 1730, probably in North Kingstown or Newport, Rhode Island.[1] His Great-grandfather George Soule arrived on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in Bristol Rhode Island 7 June 1753, Elizabeth Smith, daughter of Samuel and Elizabeth (Drown) Smith.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin died in New York in 1782, probably in Roxborough (now Grafton), Rensselaer. His estate was proved in Farmington in 1782.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin West was "of" Stonington 11 Feb 1754. Then Benjamin West of Hopkinton, Rhode Island, cordwainer, bought 6 acres in Hopkinton, 1 Dec 1760 and another 2 acres 5 Dec 1760. 25 July 1766, Benjamin, now of Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONC , and his wife Elizabeth sold six acres in Westerly, Rhode Island.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin was a member and a Deacon of the Seventh Day Baptist Church of Hopkinton.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family moved to the area of Burlington-Farmington, Connecticut before the Revolution. He and sons Benjamin jr and Hezekiah, sighed the Farmington Petition to the Connecticut legislature asking permission to labor on the first 
2 CONC day, since they celebrated the Sabbath on the seventh day.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Hezekiah West, b. 13 June 1754[1] Mary West b. c 1756[1] Child West ?? b. c 1758/9 died young ??[1] Benjamin West b. Hopkinton Rhose Island 30 Nov 1761[1] Michael West b. c. 1763[1] Child West ?? b. c. 1765; died young??[1] Thomas
2 CONC  West b. 2 March 1767[1] Rusemire/Rusimiah West b. c. 1769[1] James West//, b. c Jan 1771 (the Mayflower Society needs proof of James)[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/West-9162
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Benjamin West (1730 - 1782)===
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin West
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1730 in Westerly, Washington, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William West and Jane (Tanner) West
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of William West [half], Thomas West and Ebenezer West
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Elizabeth (Smith) West — married 7 Jun 1753 in Bristol, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Hezekiah West and Thomas West
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1782 in Exeter, Washington, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 5 Apr 2018 | Created 22 May 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
