1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Farrell K. Rose passed away Saturday, December 11, 2010 at the Washington Terrace Care Center. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrell was born January 20, 1932 in Morgan, Utah, the son of Parley August and Martha Elenor Porter Rose. He was raised in the Morgan area 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrell married Joyce Voss on March 25, 1953 in the Logan LDS Temple. Together they lived their life in Washington Terrace, South Weber and Mesquite, Nevada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints serving in many calling including Elders Quorum President and serving on the High Council. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrell worked for Hill AFB and DDO for over 35 years as a marketing and redistribution specialist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the President of the Bambrough Irrigation Ditch Company for many years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He spent many days roller-skating at Como Springs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrell was an avid fisherman. He loved gardening and always had a large garden to share with others. Farrell enjoyed woodworking, beekeeping, raising cattle, hunting with his sons, and loved to cut and gather firewood for the sto
2 CONC ve. He and Joyce loved to dance every week. He was avid rock hound. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, Joyce; three sons, Bart Rose; Guy E. (Sandy) Rose; Jeffrey N. Rose; 4 grandchildren, 14 great-grandchildren; Dan Rose; Jamie Jeppsen; Jennifer Patterson; Joni Hyer; his brother, Otis Rose; and sister, N
2 CONC atel (Ralph) Thackery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrell was preceded in death by his parents; two sons, Rees and Todd; and his sisters, Edith Peterson; Gay Johnson and Fern Evans. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family expresses sincere appreciation to Dianne Christensen, a niece, Brett and Debbie, and Hospice who helped so much
