1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NaTel Rose Thackeray
2 CONT March 8, 1936 - July 27, 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT NaTel Rose Thackeray, daughter of Parley August Rose and Martha Eleanor Porter, age 83, died July 27, 2019, in Morgan, Utah, just five days following her husband Ralph’s passing. Her six siblings preceded her in death: Edith Rose 
2 CONC Peterson, Hazel Rose, Gae Rose Johnson, Fern Rose Evans, Parley Otis Rose, and Farrell K Rose. She is survived by in-laws Paul and Romona Thackeray Dickson, JoAnne F. Thackeray, and Joyce V. Rose.
2 CONT NaTel graduated from Morgan High School. She was a devoted wife, mother, and faithful member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. She attended Weber College (now Weber State University) and Brigham Young University.
2 CONC  She married Ralph B. Thackeray on September 10, 1965, in the Salt Lake Temple. They moved to Etna, California to join the Thackeray brothers on Crystal Creek Ranch. Upon returning to Morgan in 1984, NaTel worked for the Browning 
2 CONC Arms Accounting Department. 
2 CONT She is survived by her four children, Burnett (Gina), Rosemary, Dallan (Annette), Laura Adams (Mark); six grandchildren: Callie Heiner (Austin), Laura, Porter, and Eliza Thackeray, Justin and Katie Adams; and great-granddaughter, 
2 CONC Ruby Heiner.
