2 PLAC Pinesdale Cemetery, Pinesdale, Ravalli County, Montana, USA
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamilton
3 STAE MT
3 POST 59840
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 OCT 1939
2 ADDR
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 MAY 2014
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamilton
3 STAE MT
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} PINESDALE – Louis LaMar Jessop was surrounded by his loved ones on this earth as he joined his loved ones on the other side, Friday, May 30, 2014.
2 CONT Louis LaMar, a twin to Leslie LaVar, was born Oct. 11, 1939, in Murray, Utah, to Joseph Lyman Jessop and Winnie Porter Jessop. When the boys were 6 they moved with the rest of their family to Anitmony, Utah. A few years later, Lou
2 CONC is was devastated when his beloved twin was tragically killed in an accident. Louis missed Leslie the rest of his life. In 1958 Louis graduated from Murray High School and in 1961 Louis began his own family. From that day on his f
2 CONC amily was high on his list of priorities. Not a day went by that he didn't express his love and devotion to every member of his family. Because he was such a good father, her acted as a father figure to nieces, nephews, daughters-
2 CONC in-law, sons-in-law and even several who where not related to him. Everyone loved Lou and he was definitely a "favorite."
2 CONT Lou's favorite pastime was helping others and tinkering to fix things. No one could fix things up like he could, using nuts, bolts, duct tape or anything else he had at his disposal. He was truly a master of odd jobs. When asked f
2 CONC or his help, Lou's fee was usually free. He helped strictly out of his love for other people.
2 CONT His family lived in many places, but finally settled in Pinesdale, where Lou eventually became head maintenance/custodial personnel at Pines Academy. The children there loved him dearly and his calming, peaceful, helping presence 
2 CONC will be sorely missed. Lou's life was devoted to two things: His Father in heaven and his family, which to him was heaven on earth. As he leaves this world to continue his work on the other side, his family sends their love and su
2 CONC pport with him. His all-enveloping hugs will be missed by everyone. He leaves behind a family that is strong, loving, large and devoted.
2 CONT Viewing is at Pines Academy Sunday, June 1 and Monday, noon-1:30 p.m. Funeral is Monday at 2 p.m at the Pines Academy. Condolences may be left for the family at www.dalyleachchapel.com.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/132124631/louis-lamar-jessop Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 24 2023, 13:27:46 UTC''
