1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was born June 15, 1914, at Basalt, to Earl Gregg and Mabel Porter Frandsen. She attended schools in Ogden, Utah and graduated from Ogden High School. She attended Weber State College.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Dec. 22, 1933 she married Heber Allen Sellers in the Salt Lake LDS Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was an active member of the LDS Church and served as Relief Society president. She was an accomplished musician and served as stake organist for 28 years. She taught piano lessons and was choir organist. She enjoyed sewing, wr
2 CONC iting poetry and attending the temple.
2 CONT
