1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fern Rose McBride, 94, died Friday, October 13, 2006, in St. George, Washington County, Utah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on May 7, 1912, in Smoot, Wyoming. Her parents were Leander Armstead Moffett and Rose Hannah Gomm Moffett. She married Cleao Wells McBride in Burley, Idaho, on June 5, 1928, and they were sealed in the Salt Lake LDS T
2 CONC emple on June 7, 1928 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband; parents; four brothers; one sister; and her son, Richard, preceded her in death. She is survived by her children, Ramon McBride of Burley, Earl McBride of Kaysville, Utah, Rosemary Hoggan of Washington, Utah, Ruth Bud
2 CONC ge of St. George, Utah, Jay McBride of Rupert, Gerald McBride of Prescott, Ariz., Rex McBride of Burbank, Calif., Karma Smith of West Jordan, Utah, Janell Jenkins of Polo, Mo., and Sherrie Gardner of Bountiful, Utah; 59 grandchild
2 CONC ren; 112 great-grandchildren; and 16 great-great-grandchildren. Her surviving brother and sisters are Russell Charles Moffett, Ruth Mary Machen and Joye Nellie Brough.
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended Burley schools and was a devoted member of the LDS Church, having faithfully served in many capacities during her life. As a talented musician, she provided music for various church services, community programs, weddi
2 CONC ngs and funerals for more than 75 years. She and her husband fulfilled a church mission in the Fresno, Calif., mission and also served in the St. George Temple. They celebrated their 72nd wedding anniversary in June 2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements were under the direction of Rasmussen Funeral Home in Burley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published Times-News, The (Twin Falls, ID) - October 17, 2006
