1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ruth Mary (Moffett) Machen passed away Friday, Feb. 25, 2011, at Cherry Ridge of Emmett. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth was born in Burley, Idaho, Oct. 7, 1925. Ruth was married to Leon Harold Machen in Hamer, Idaho, Nov. 3, 1942, and sealed a year later in the Idaho Falls Temple. They had their 68th wedding anniversary together at Cherry Ridg
2 CONC e this past November. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth had a variety of jobs from telephone switchboard operator to selling figurette bras, to being a legal secretary, which she thoroughly enjoyed. She worked in the law office of Smith, Miller and Weston, the Canyon County Sherif
2 CONC f's Dept., the judicial office of Judge Jones in Canyon County and was actively involved in the Canyon County Republican party.
2 CONT
2 CONT In all her jobs and in her life – she loved working and spending time with others. Ruth enjoyed baseball, square dancing, ceramics and many other activities. Most of all, she loved spending time with her family. In the Church of J
2 CONC esus Christ of Latter-day Saints, Ruth served in many capacities, largely, with the youth and in the Relief Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth is preceded in death by her parents, Leander and Rose Moffett; her five brothers, Leonard, William, Robert, Rex and Russell; two of her sisters, Fern and Nelda and is survived by her youngest sister, Joye Brough, of Ogden, Ut
2 CONC ah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth is also survived by her husband, Leon Harold Machen; her two daughters, Gay Weaver (Jack) and Monica Buchanan (Brent); her grandchildren, Cassandra Sorg (Brent), Jaclyn Silbernagel (Cassidy), Daniel Buchanan (Amanda), Nicole 
2 CONC Still (Tanner), Natalie and Anna Buchanan; and her four great-grandchildren, Joshua, Adam, Samuel and Britynn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She will be lovingly remembered by all who knew her but especially by her family. Ruth's family wishes to express their gratitude to all who have touched her life and most recently to the staff at Cherry Ridge and the members of t
2 CONC he Middleton 1st Ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT There will be a viewing at the LDS Middleton Stake Center (23644 Old Hwy 30) Tuesday, March 1, 2011, from 5-9 p.m. and also Wednesday from 12-12:50 p.m. The service will be held Wednesday, March 2, 2011, at 1 p.m. at the Middleton
2 CONC  Stake Center as mentioned above. Services are with the Potter Funeral Chapel of Emmett.
