1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daily Post Athenian Aug 15, 210
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell G. Moffett, Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell G. "Russ" Moffett Sr., 82, of Athens, died Sunday night, Aug. 15, 2010, at his residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a native of Burley, Idaho, and was a former resident of Findlay, Ohio. He was a resident of Athens for the last 12 years and attended Trinity United Methodist Church. A son of the late Leander and Hannah Rose Gomm Moffett, 
2 CONC he was preceded in death by four brothers, Leonard, William, Robert and Rex Moffett; and two sisters, Fern McBride and Nelda Schwabb.
2 CONT
2 CONT A graduate of the University of Idaho, he played football and was quarterback during the team's upset victory over Stanford University on Sept. 27, 1947. He recently attended the 50-year anniversary celebrating the momentous win. 
2 CONC A veteran of the U.S. Navy, he retired as naval commander after 27 years of service, having served during both the Korean War and the Vietnam War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife of 27 years, Margie Becknell Moffett of Athens; two daughters, Katheryn Kortier of Rossford, Ohio, and Suzy Moffett of Perrysburg, Ohio; one son, Russell Moffett Jr. of the city of Dubai on the Persian G
2 CONC ulf; three grandchildren, Anna Kortier, Elyse Kortier and Benjamin Stalets; two sisters and one brother-in-law, Ruth and Leon Machen of Caldwell, Idaho, and Joye Brough of Riverdale, Utah; and many loving extended family members.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be 7 p.m. Thursday at Ziegler Funeral Home with Hospice Chaplain Don Sapp officiating. Graveside services with full military honors will be 11 a.m. Saturday at Rose Hill Burial Park in Hamilton, Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family will receive friends from 5 to 7 p.m. Thursday at the funeral home.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, the family suggests memorial contributions be made to The Wounded Warrior Project, National Processing Center, P.O. Box 758516, Topeka, KS 66675-8516.
