1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eliza Franklin married Peter Betts in the Church by Banns, April 28, 1822. Peter was a blacksmith and spring maker by trade who immigrated to the U.SA. before other members of his family. In October 1850, Eliza and
2 CONC  her children left England to join her husband and their father. They sailed on the ship James Pennell and landed in New Orleans. From there they went to St. Louis, MO. They used the perpetual immigration fund to make the journey.
2 CONC  Her husband died in St. Louis August 28, 1863
