1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George married Elizabeth Hall Mills, a widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was very beautiful. She never told her age and was always "just 40." Lonely, she met and married George Rowley. She was five years older than George. They had two sons. They moved to Huntsville and then to Soda Springs n
2 CONC ear Bear Lake. George Rowley left Elizabeth and the Church. Elizabeth died the 20th of January 1900 and was buried in Soda Springs. 
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Bennington, Bear Lake, Idaho, United States - June 14 1880
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Soda Springs Village, Bannock, Idaho, United States - June 1900
