1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Folsom Wilson
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 ~ 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (Bob) Folsom Wilson, 87, died May 17, 2008, in Provo, Utah. He was born September 21, 1920, in Logan, Utah, to Ellis Ricks and Florence Folsom Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was preceded in death by his parents and a younger brother, David. He is survived by his three sisters, Joyce, Janice and Donna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Ruby Hartvigsen on July 26, 1946 in the Logan LDS Temple. They are the parents of Barbara Ann, Ronald (Connie), Ralph, Roger, Elaine Rydalch (Brett) and Diane Hoffer (Berkley). Robert and Ruby have 13 grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert graduated from Utah State University in 1942, and then served in the Corps of Engineers during World War II, where he was severely wounded and received a Purple Heart. He later graduated from Harvard University with a degre
2 CONC e in Public Administration. He worked for the Bureau of Reclamation, State Department and The Upper Colorado River Commission.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert blessed the lives of many people, in many different ways. He will be greatly missed. He loved serving in The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. He served with Ruby as a missionary in the Boston, Massachusetts Miss
2 CONC ion, and he also served in the Salt Lake City LDS Temple and the Mt. Timpanogos LDS Temple for many years. Robert enjoyed traveling to many different places and he also loved landscape photography, taking many beautiful pictures.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Wed., May 21, 2008 at 11 a.m. in the Highland 13th Ward Chapel, 5848 W. 11000 N. (Highland Highway), Highland, Utah. A viewing will be held Tues. evening from 7-8:30 p.m. at the Walker Sanderson Funer
2 CONC al Home, 646 E. 800 N., Orem, Utah and Wed. one hour prior to the funeral at the church. Burial will be in the Bountiful City Cemetery. Condolences may be sent
2 CONT
2 CONT to the family at: www.walkerfamilymortuary.com
