1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Vivian Nadine Folsom Taylor 1924 ~ 2008 Vivian Nadine Folsom Taylor, loving wife, mother, grandmother and great-grandmother, passed away November 13, 2008 of natural causes. She was born September 27, 1924 in Salt
2 CONC  Lake City, UT to Lily Allen Folsom and Paul Whitaker Folsom. In 1942 she met John Merle Taylor in their Latin 4 class at East High School. They were high school sweethearts and married on August 3, 1945 in the Logan LDS temple. V
2 CONC ivian loved to read and had an unquenchable thirst for knowledge. She was always ready to talk about the latest book she'd read or class she's taken. She inspired and encouraged her children and grandchildren to gain a good educat
2 CONC ion and was always willing and happy to talk to them about what they were learning. She loved birds, music, art, the color blue and knitting. Her hands were always busy making a sweater or blanket for someone. Vivian was a member 
2 CONC of the Daughters of the Utah Pioneers and a faithful member of the LDS church where she served in many capacities but was most distinguished as a great teacher. Her love of music brought joy to her life and for several years she s
2 CONC ang with the Melodine chorus. She was an exceptional secretary and worked for the Utah Association of Counties and the Utah board of Regents for higher education. Vivian was loved and respected by all who knew her. She was truly a
2 CONC  great lady and her influence on her family is immeasurable. Vivian is survived by her husband John Merle Taylor, her brother Theron Folsom (Judy), her daughters, Susan Wilcox and Laurie Williams (Scott), her son Keith Folsom Tayl
2 CONC or, 12 grandchildren and 17 great-grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her father Paul W. Folsom, her mother, Lily Folsom and her brother Hugh Folsom. Memorial Services celebrating Vivian's life will be held at the Salt Lak
2 CONC e Little Cottonwood 16th Ward, 6350 So. Rodeo Lane (1540 E.) at 12 noon, Monday, Nov. 17, 2008. Friends and family may pay their respects at Larkin Mortuary, 260 E. South Temple, Salt Lake City, Utah on Sunday, Nov. 16, 2008 from 
2 CONC 6-8 p.m. and one hour prior to services at the church. Our special thanks to hospice and the staff at Wentworth Assisted Living for the loving care they gave her. Online condolences at www.larkincares.com 
