1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bruce Folsom Hillam
2 CONT
2 CONT July 30, 1920-April 19, 2004
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruce Folsom Hillam, 83, of Vista died Monday. He was born in Salt Lake City and was a retired lieutenant colonel in the Marine Corps. He was a veteran of World War II and the Korean War. He was a member of the Vista school board,
2 CONC  the Boy Scouts and Rotary International.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, Harriett Parks Hillam; daughters, Robyn Moravetz of Woodbury, Minn., Deborah Bylo of Ventura and Ann Finney of Oceanside; son, Bruce Parks Hillam of La Verne; sisters, Shirley Nielsen of Orem, Utah, and
2 CONC  June Bertram of St. George, Utah; brother, Duane Hillam of Provo, Utah; and five grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services: 11 a.m. Saturday, Allen Bros. Mortuary, 1315 S. Santa Fe Ave., Vista.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment: 2 p.m. May 1, Salt Lake City Cemetery, 200 N St., Salt Lake City, Utah. Published in San Diego Union-Tribune on April 22, 2004
2 CONT
