1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shirley May Folsom Hillam Nielsen passed away peacefully on Monday, November 17, 2014. She lived a grand and dedicated life, full of service to her husband, family, ward family, friends, neighbors and Savior. She w
2 CONC as married to Jay L. Nielsen for 48 years before he passed away in 1994. Jay and Shirley raised four children, Paul, Ruth Ann, Dean and Ray. Our mother grew up in Salt Lake City where she loved to be with her sister, June and two 
2 CONC brothers, Bruce and Duane, all loyal South High Alumni. Shirley was an outstanding cook, a stellar artist in watercolor and acrylics, a seamstress and quilt maker extraordinaire. She was a member of the Quilters Guild. Mother also
2 CONC  sang in her ward choir and played a mean piano. She had a strong testimony of the gospel and served in numerous church positions. Any time our mother sat down, she was working on making hats from her abundant supply of yarn and h
2 CONC at loom. Mother made over two thousand hats and donated them to humanitarian groups. She also created the infamous "Lunch Bunch" group in her ward, where the widows would pick a restaurant and enjoy each others company. Shirley wa
2 CONC s always proud of and checked on her children, grand and great-grandchildren regularly. She loved attending their numerous programs of dancing, sporting events and band performances. She taught elementary school (2nd grade) in Jor
2 CONC dan School District for 22 years. During WW2, she worked making radio tubes to support the war effort. She was always dependable, loved to travel and enjoyed family and church parties. She made it a point to welcome new people int
2 CONC o the neighborhood with homemade treats. She is survived by her sister, June Bertram, her four children: Paul (Donna), Ruth Ann, Dean (Lynne) and Ray (Judy). She was very proud of her 13 grandchildren and 13 great grandchildren wi
2 CONC th twins on the way. We have been so greatly blessed to have you teach and influence our lives with your wonderful example of charity and service. 'Til we meet again Mother, With Love, Your Family.  Funeral services will be Mon., 
2 CONC Nov. 24, 2014 in the Orem Cascade 1st Ward Chapel, 473 E. Center St. at 11 a.m. Viewings will be Sunday, Nov. 23rd from 6-8 p.m. at the Walker Sanderson Funeral Home, 646 East 800 North, Orem, and Monday morning from 10-10:45 a.m.
2 CONC  at the church. Interment will be in the Orem City Cemetery. Condolences may be offered to the family online at www.walkersanderson.com.
