1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lila F. Willis, died May 25,2009. She was born July 8, 1927, in Vancouver, B.C. and grew up in Utah. She graduated from Davis High School in Kaysville, UT and attended Brigham Young University where she met Glen H.
2 CONC  Tolman. In 1946 they were married in Salt Lake City,UT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in Utah and Idaho before moving to Hermiston, OR and then to Olympia, WA in 1956 with their three daughters. In Olympia, Lila Tolman worked at Andersen's Greenhouse, and later for the State of Washington. She enjoyed mu
2 CONC sic and played the viola in the Olympia Symphony. She also encouraged her daughters and friends in music. For many years she conducted singing at church and taught basic music skills. She filled her time with church service, sewin
2 CONC g, knitting, and reading. She was a charter member and officer of the Capitol Camp of the Daughters of Utah Pioneers.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1972, Lila married John B. Willis. After retirement, they enjoyed many activities and traveling together, especially in Mexico.  They were blessed with 12 years together before John's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She later married Eb Eldredge, her high school sweetheart. Survivors include daughters Glenna Olson (Erick) of Kelso; Ann Wilde (Alan) of Anchorage, Alaska; and Lynn Urvina (Lars) of Lacey; 13 grandchildren; 20 great-grandchildren
2 CONC ; siblings Marvin Folsom (Ruth) of Provo,UT; Iris Rosenberg of Colorado Springs, CO; Jerry H. Folsom(Geraldine) of West Jordan, UT; and Nancy Weinheimer (Gordon) of Ivins, UT.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lila Willis is preceded in death by her first-born daughter, Kay Tolman (1951); John B. Willis (1984); and her parents, Donald Whitaker Folsom and Ellen Rose Binns Folsom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be on Monday, June 1, 2009 from 9:30-10:30 am with funeral services following at 11:00 am at The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, 3800 Henderson Boulevard, Olympia, WA.  Burial will follow in the Pionee
2 CONC r Section of Woodlawn Cemetery, Lacey, WA.
