1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Iris Josephine (Folsom) Carey was born in Salt Lake City, Utah on April 23rd, 1930. She passed away on December 22, 2009 in Colorado Springs, CO. Iris grew up in Centerville, UT where she was active in Glee Club an
2 CONC d the High School choir. She moved to California where she raised her children and worked for the State of California. Iris and her long-time partner, Charles Rosenthal, spent 17 years in Mexico where they built a house on lake Ch
2 CONC apala and guided tours through old Mexico and central Mexico. Upon moving to Colorado Springs, Iris and Charles were active for 18 years in the Stratmoor Hills Neighborhood Association. She spent many hours decorating her house fo
2 CONC r the holidays, especially Christmas. She handcrafted over 90 miniature hot air balloons which she proudly displayed each Labor Day in support of the Colorado Springs Hot Air Balloon Festival. Above all, Iris's favorite past time 
2 CONC and what brought her the most joy was her family. She will be dearly missed. She is survived by her brothers: Marvin and Jerry Folsom; sister, Nancy Weinheimer all of Utah; her loving children: Kristine Betts (husband, Gary) of Co
2 CONC lorado Springs; Doug (wife, Beverly) Youngberg of Sprague River, OR; Mike Youngberg (wife, Brenda) of Atlanta, GA; Valerie Tipton (husband, Kevan) of Roseville, CA; 10 grandchildren, 22 great-grandchildren; and 1 great-great grand
2 CONC child. Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. on Tuesday, December 29, 2009 at the Shrine of Remembrance America the Beautiful Chapel, with visitation one hour prior to services. Interment will follow at Evergreen Cemetery. - See
2 CONC  more at: http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/gazette/obituary.aspx?n=iris-josephine-carey&pid=137843788#sthash.WeL55U4j.dpuf
