2 CONT PROVO DAILY HERALD, Provo, UT, Sunday, August 20, 1972, page 4: "Margaret Cloward. Payson --- Margaret Maria Terry Mendenhall Cloward, 86, of Payson died Thursday at the home of a daughter in Santaquin. "She was born on April 30, 
2 CONC in Fairview, Sanpete County, to Charles A. and Margaret Ann Anderson Terry. She married Jesse Mendenhall in 1904 in Raymond, Alberta, Canada. He died in 1922. She then married Orson Pratt Cloward on Aug. 10, 1922 in the Salt Lake 
2 CONC LDS Temple. He died on Jan 6, 1937. "She was a member of the LDS Church and held offices in the Primary, Sunday School, and Relief Society. She was also an active genealogy worker. "She is survived b y sons and daughters, Wendell 
2 CONC Terry Mendenhall, San Diego, Calif.; Lee Mendenhall, Provo; Rex Mendenhall, Mrs. Leon (Thelma) Taylor, Mrs. Ruel (Gladys) Clayson, all of Payson; Mrs. James (Ladora) Brady, Santaquin; Mrs. Bert (Zeld) Tuttle, Long Beach, Calif.; M
2 CONC rs. LeRoy (Nina) Robinson, Chula Vista, Calif.; Mrs. Don (Jessie) Mangum, San Diego; several grandchildren; sisters, Mrs.. Arch Pulham, Provo; Mrs. Lynn Lance, Salt Lake City. "Funeral services will be Monday at 1 p.m. in the Pays
2 CONC on Nebo LDS Stake Center. Friends may call at the Rigby Mortuary in Payson today from 7 p.m. to 9 p.m. and Monday before the services. Burial will be in the Provo City Cemetery." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
