2 _MARNM Smith
1 NAME Oliver Rollin Smith
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 MAR 1913
2 ADDR
3 CITY Davenport
3 STAE IA
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1990
2 ADDR
3 CITY Provo
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE 17 DEC 1990
2 PLAC Provo, Utah, Utah
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sharing our Links to the Past by Wally and Frances Gray
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Rollin Smith 1913-1990
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bushman Family History by Newbern Butt, pp. 170
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Rollin Smith, born 8 March 1913, Davenport, Iowa.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: Salt Lake City, Colorado Springs, Provo.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Attended the University of Utah; graduated from BYU (B.A.); PhD. from the University of Iowa.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Professor of Journalism, BYU President of Chapter Delta Phi; National editor of their journal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Served in World War II as a Captain in the Air Corps, U. S., Philippines and Japan.  In ROTC 1946 to date.  President of MIA at BYU; Mission to the Eastern States 1934-36; mission publicity director; High Councilman, East Provo St
2 CONC ake 1947; member of the Granite Stake MIA Board 1933-34; Counselor in Iowa Branch, Northern States Mission; teacher in MIA, Palmyra and Casper Branches; member Utah Parks Council of Boy Scouts 1938-40.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 6 April 1942, Salt Lake Temple, Barbara Fay McKay, daughter of Thomas Evans McKay and Fawn Brimhall.  She was born 2 October 1920, Ogden, Utah.  She attended BYU; member of Lambda Delta Sigma officers.  Mission to Switz
2 CONC erland 1937-39.
2 CONT
2 CONT ©1998-2008 Wallace F. and Frances M. Gray. This web page may be freely linked. To contact us send to grayfox2@cox.net  Their home page is http://www.geocities.com/wallygray25/index.html 1
