1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Alonzo Kimball Wood— Mendon, Alonzo Kimball Wood, 86, lifelong Mendon resident, died Monday. He was born April 25, 1887, in Mendon, a son of Joseph Turner and Julia Kimball Wood. He married Florence Annett Bowen September 9, 1914 
2 CONC in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. She died August 27, 1967. Mr. Wood was a member of the Mendon LDS Ward, and a high priest in Logan Stake. He served in the ward Sunday School superintendency for 15 years, had been a stake missionary, 
2 CONC and chairman of the old folks committee. He played second violin with the University orchestra for five years, was a landscape gardener, local agent for Stark Brothers Nursery for 40 years, and had received an award of his merchan
2 CONC dising service. Surviving are four daughters one son: Mrs. Claude (Lea) Staples, Logan; Mrs. Ed (Lorraine) Muir, Tremonton; Mrs. Bill (Dorothy) Richeson, Salt Lake City; Mrs. Marlin (Juanita) Larsen, Layton, and Alonzo Gilbert Woo
2 CONC d, Los Angeles, California; 13 grandchildren; 19 great-grandchildren. Funeral services will be conducted Thursday noon in Mendon Ward chapel by Bishop Stanton E. Barrett. Friends may call at Hall Mortuary Wednesday from 7 to 9 p.m
2 CONC ., and at the Mendon chapel Thursday one hour prior to funeral. Burial will be in Mendon Cemetery.  [The Herald Journal, October 23, 1973, page 4]
