1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hunt_Udall
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hunt Udall (August 23, 1889 – March 3, 1959) was mayor of Phoenix, Arizona from 1936 to 1938. He was a member of the Udall political family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of David King Udall and Ida Frances (Hunt) Udall, he was born and raised in Arizona. He was a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a cattleman and farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ruth Kimball, sister of Spencer W. Kimball in 1912. They had a son, Nick. Ruth died in 1915. In 1916, he remarried to Leah Smith, daughter of Jesse Nathaniel Smith. He and Leah had several more children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1922 he was elected as clerk of the Arizona Superior Court, defeating his younger brother Levi Stewart Udall.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1936 to 1938 he served as mayor of Phoenix. He also served in the Arizona State Legislature.
2 CONT
2 CONT He sought, but was defeated for the Republican nomination for Governor of Arizona. In 1948 he was narrowly defeated as the Republican candidate for the U.S. House of Representatives from the Arizona 1st District.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Mesa, Arizona in 1959.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Nick Udall served as Mayor of Phoenix from 1948 to 1952.
