1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=108349 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jan. 31, 1906 Farmington Davis County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Sep. 26, 1971 Farmington Davis County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of David Cornelius Hess and Lois Catherine Kimball
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Septimus Herman Buchholz, 7 Aug 1926, Coalville, Summit, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Son - Stanley Buchholz Kimball
2 CONT
2 CONT History - Vontella Bulcholz Kimball was born in Farmington, Utah in 1906. She was the great-granddaughter of Heber C. Kimball, daughter of Corneilius Hess, and mother of Stanley Bucholz Kimball. Although there are a few references
2 CONC  to her personal life, Vontella mentions she married a distant cousin by the name of Kimball.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vontella was seventeen years of age, she enrolled at the University of Utah in Salt Lake City and was employed in the cosmetics department of Auerbachs, a local department store. Newspaper clippings indicate that she was a ha
2 CONC ndsome woman. She more or less created the job she later held being Helena Rubenstein in 1935. She lectured on charm and beauty at Brigham Young University in 1959. Her subject was titled "Beauty Through the Ages."
2 CONT
2 CONT In the course of her work, she visited the Middle East six times, starting in 1935. Her admiration for the Arab world kept her in contact with the friends and customs she encountered on her many trips. Later, she gave lectures in 
2 CONC the United States in Arab costumes and jewelry. She lectured for 20 years and then went to radio and television.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vontella Kimball died in 1971. 
2 CONT
